('POL-HC-8462', 'CranMax®', 'CranMax&reg; prevent adhesion of E. coli to the uroepithelial cells in women which is a risk factor for developing urinary tract infections.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-8463', 'A combination of L-threonine, L-valine, L-leucine, L-isoleucine, L-lysine plus chromium picolinate', 'Contributes to the reduction of the blood glucose rise when consumed together with a carbohydrate rich meal.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8464', 'Bimuno® GOS', 'Regular daily consumption of 1,37 g galacto-oligosaccharides from Bimuno&reg; may reduce adbominal discomfort', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8465', 'Beta-alanine', 'Beta-alanine increases performance during short-duration high intensity exercise', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8520', 'Coffee C21, a blend of pure Arabica roast coffees ( Coffea arabica L.) without any non-coffee ingredients', 'Regular consumption of Coffee C21 contributes to the maintenance of DNA integrity in cells of the body', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8521', 'Carbohydrate solutions', 'Carbohydrate solutions contribute to the improvement of physical performance during a high-intensity and long-lasting physical exercise in trained adults.', 'The claim may be used only for carbohydrate solutions which, according to the instructions of use, provide between 30 g and 90 g of carbohydrates/hour, where the carbohydrates in question are glucose, sucrose, fructose and/or maltodextrins, under the following conditions: a) Fructose (from fructose and/or sucrose) should not represent more than 1/3 of total carbohydrates, and b) Glucose (from glucose, sucrose and/or maltodextrins) should not exceed 60 g/h. Information shall be given to the consumer that the beneficial effect is obtained only by trained adults performing high-intensity (at least at 65 % of the VO2max) and long-lasting (at least 60 min) physical exercise. The claim may be used only for foods intended for trained adults performing high-intensity and long-lasting physical exercise.', null, 'authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8522', 'Bifidobacterium animalis subsp. lactis (Bi‐07)', 'Biﬁdobacterium animalis subsp. lactis Bi-07 contributes to the improvement of lactose digestion in individuals who have difficulty digesting lactose', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8523', 'MenaQ7 ® , vitamin K2 as menaquinone-7', 'MenaQ7 ® , vitamin K2 as menaquinone-7, improves arterial stiffness', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8466', 'Standardised aqueous extract from white kidney bean ( Phaseolus vulgaris L.)', 'Helps to reduce body weight', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8467', 'A combination of lutein and zeaxanthin', 'Lutein together with zeaxanthin helps maintain clarity and contrast of sight in bright light conditions.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8468', 'Carbohydrate solutions', 'Carbohydrate solutions contribute to the maintenance of endurance performance during prolonged endurance exercice.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8524', 'Anxiofit-1, a food ingredient that contains an Echinacea angustifolia hydro-alcoholic root dry extract standardised for the specific alkamide profile', 'Anxioﬁt-1 has been shown to ameliorate subthreshold and mild anxiety. Subthreshold and mild anxiety are risk factors in the development of anxiety disorders and depression', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-8469', 'Lactobacillus plantarum TENSIA� in the semi-hard Edam-type', 'Regular, at least for eight week consumption of 50 g/day Lactobacillus plantarum TENSIA&reg; comprising S&uuml;damejuust (English translation: Heart cheese) of the Harmony&trade; brand helps to maintain the cardio-vascular system/heart health through reduction of blood pressure/Symbol of heart.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8470', 'High-fibre sourdough rye bread', 'Reduction of post-prandial glycaemic responses compared with glucose', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8471', 'Beta-galactosidase from Streptococcus thermophilus', 'Lactase for comfortable digestion', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(b)'),
('POL-HC-8472', 'Calcium', 'Calcium helps to reduce the loss of bone mineral in post-menopausal women. Low bone mineral density is a risk factor for osteoporotic bone fractures', 'The claim may be used only for food which provides at least 400 mg of calcium per quantified portion. Information shall be given to the consumer that the claim is specifically intended for women 50 years and older and the beneficial effect is obtained with a daily intake of at least 1 200 mg of calcium from all sources. For foods with added calcium the claim may be used only for those targeting women 50 years and older', null, 'authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-8473', 'Non-digestible oligo- and polysaccharides including galacto- oligosaccharides, oligofructose, polyfructose and inulin', 'With non-digestible oligo- and/ or polysaccharides to stimulate calcium absorption', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(b)'),
('POL-HC-8474', 'Prunes', 'Dried plums/prunes can contribute to normal bowel function', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(b)'),
('POL-HC-8475', 'Fat-free yogurts and fermented milks with live yogurt cultures complying with the specifications', 'Fat-free yogurts and fermented milks with live yogurt cultures, with added vitamin D, and with no added sugars, help to reduce body and visceral fat in the context of an energy-restricted diet', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8476', 'Fat-free yogurts and fermented milks with live yogurt cultures complying with the specifications', 'Fat-free yogurts and fermented milks with live yogurt cultures, with added vitamin D, and with no added sugars, help to maintain lean body mass (muscle and bone) in the context of an energy-restricted diet', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8477', 'Teestar™, a fenugreek seed extract standardised by its content of galactomannan', 'Teestar&trade; lowers blood glucose levels', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8478', 'Clarinol® and Tonalin®', 'The consumption of Clarinol&reg; or Tonalin&reg; contributes to a reduction in body fat mass.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8479', 'Native chicory inulin', 'Chicory inulin contributes to normal bowel function by increasing stool frequency', 'Information shall be provided to the consumer that the beneficial effect is obtained with a daily intake of 12 g chicory inulin. The claim can be used only for food which provides at least a daily intake of 12 g of native chicory inulin, a non-fractionated mixture of monosaccharides ( or = 9.', null, 'authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8480', 'L-tug lycopene', 'L-tug lycopene has been shown to lower/reduce blood cholesterol. High cholesterol is a risk faactor in the developent of coronary heart disease', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-8481', 'Bifidobacterium bifidum CNCM I-3426', 'Bifidobacterium bifidum CNCM I-3426 increases the proportion of healthy days by maintaining normal immune function in healthy adults during everyday life events such as moderate stress.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8482', 'SYNBIO®', 'SYNBIO&reg; persists in the intestinal tract and favours the natural regularity contributing to maintain and improve human intestinal well-being', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8483', 'Vitamin D', 'Vitamin D contributes to the normal function of the immune system in children.', 'The claim may be used only for food which is at least a source of vitamin D as referred to in the claim SOURCE OF [NAME OF VITAMIN/S] AND/OR [NAME OF MINERAL/S] as listed in the Annex to Regulation (EC) No 1924/2006.', null, 'authorised', '14(1)(b)'),
('POL-HC-08781', 'Xanthohumol in XERME®, a xanthohumol-enriched roasted malt extract', 'Helps to maintain the integrity of DNA and protects against oxidative damage in the cells of the body.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8525', 'A combination of artichoke leaf dry extract standardised in caffeoylquinic acids, monacolin K in red yeast rice, sugar-cane derived policosanols, procyanidolic oligomers from French maritime pine bark, garlic dry extract standardised in allicin, d-α-tocopheryl hydrogen succinate, riboflavin and inositol hexanicotinate', 'A combination of artichoke leaf dry extract standardised in caffeoylquinic acids, monacolin K in red yeast rice, sugar-cane derived policosanols, procyanidolic oligomers from French maritime pine bark, garlic dry extract standardised in allicin, d-α-tocopheryl hydrogen succinate, riboflavin and inositol hexanicotinate reduces blood LDL-cholesterol concentrations. High LDL-cholesterol is a risk factor in the development of coronary heart disease', 'The claim may be used only for food supplements which provide 600 mg artichoke leaf dry extract with 30-36 mg caffeoylquinic acids, 500 mg red yeast rice with 2 mg monacolin K, 10 mg sugar-cane derived policosanols, 20 mg French maritime pine bark extract with 18 mg procyanidolic oligomers, 30 mg garlic dry extract with 0,25 mg allicin, 30 mg α-tocopherol equivalents, 5 mg riboflavin and 9 mg inositol hexanicotinate divided in three daily doses to be consumed with the major meals.', null, 'authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-08741', 'Beta-glucans sourced from oats and/or barley, incorporated into ready-to-eat breakfast cereals manufactured via pressure cooking (i.e.either by batch cooking or extrusion), and present at a level of at least 1,3 g per 25 g available carbohydrate in the ready-to-eat cereal', 'Consumption of beta-glucans from oats and/or barley in a ready-to-eat breakfast cereal contributes to a reduction of the blood glucose rise after that meal', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-08601', 'Organic foods', 'Organic food (lower levels of pesticide residues than those in conventional food) contributes to the protection of body cells and molecules (lipids and DNA) from oxidative damage', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(b)'),
('POL-HC-08743', 'MegaNatural®-BP grape seed extract made entirely of California-grown grapes containing biologically active constituents: total phenolics (90–93 %), gallic acid (≥ 2 %) and catechin and epicatechin (≥ 5 %). The distribution of phenolic compounds in the MegaNatural®-BP is on average 9 % monomers, 69 % oligomers and 22 % polymers', 'MegaNatural®-BP helps maintain healthy blood pressure', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-08744', 'Frutalose® chicory oligofructose', 'Frutalose® chicory oligofructose contributes to regular bowel function by increasing stool frequency (And three other alternative wordings)', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-08742', 'Affron®, aqueous saffron extract, with the sum of crocins and safranal concentration > 3,5 % and dextrin as inert carrier', 'Affron® contributes to maintain a healthy mood by reducing the negative traits of depressive and anxiety feelings', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-11241', 'Monacolin K in SYLVAN BIO red yeast rice', 'Monacolin K from red yeast rice contributes to the maintenance of normal blood LDL-cholesterol concentrations', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8450', 'Caffeine', 'Caffeine helps to increase alertness* * For intakes of caffeine between 40 mg per serving and 75 mg per serving', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8518', 'A combination of beta-sitosterol and beta-sitosterol glucoside', 'Contributes to the normal function of the immune system by restoring balance between TH1- and TH2- mediated immunity', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-12721', 'Appethyl®, an aqueous extract from spinach leaves standardised by the manufacturing process and its lipase/colipase inhibition capacity in vitro', 'Appethyl® helps your body weight reduction during mild caloric restriction', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8217', 'Zinc', 'Zinc supports a healthy thyroid function. Zinc is beneficial for the thyroid function.', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(1)'),
('POL-HC-14785', 'Joselito® ham', 'Consumption of Joselito® ham reduces blood LDL-cholesterol concentration or blood pressure', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(a)'),
('POL-HC-08721', 'Green kiwifruit (Actinidia deliciosa (var. Hayward))', 'Consumption of green kiwifruit contributes to normal bowel function by increasing stool frequency', 'The claim may be used only for: (i)fresh green kiwifruits sold as such, or (ii)fresh green kiwifruits which have only been peeled and/or cut providing a minimum of 200 g of kiwi flesh. Information shall be given to the consumer that the beneficial effect is obtained with a daily intake of 200 g of fresh green kiwi flesh.', null, 'authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-14782', 'Citicoline (CDP-Choline) inner salt', 'Citicoline supports improvement, maintenance or reduced loss of memory in healthy middle-aged or elderly adults encountering age-associated subjective memory impairment', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8512', 'Black tea from Camellia sinensis', 'Improves endothelium-dependent vasodilation, which contributes to healthy blood flow', null, null, 'non_authorised', '13(5)'),
('POL-HC-8451', 'Plant sterol esters', 'Plant sterol esters presented as food supplement in powder sachet have been shown to lower/reduce blood cholesterol. High cholesterol is a risk factor in the development of coronary heart disease', null, null, 'non_authorised', '14(1)(a)')
insert into public.eu_novel_food_status (code, name, synonyms, common_names, parts, description) values
('POL-NF-15501', 'Hemidesmus indicus (L.) R.Br.', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Hemidesmus indicus (L.) R.Br., commonly called Indian sarsaparilla, is a slender, twining to semi erect medicinal shrub native to the Indian subcontinent and Southeast Asia.'),
('POL-NF-11602', 'Non-isolated fulvic acid', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns non-isolated fulvic acid . According to the conclusion reached by the Lithuanian competent authorities, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, non-isolated fulvic acid is considered novel food .'),
('POL-NF-15401', 'Vicia faba', null, null, '[{"part":"Malted fava bean powder","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns malted fava bean ( Vicia faba L.) powder. The request was submitted to the Irish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-11801', 'Pinus halepensis Mill.', 'Pinus maritima Aiton.; Pinus maritima Mill.', null, '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Green pinecones and the bark","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns seeds, green pinecones and the bark of the plant species Pinus halepensis Mill. The request was submitted to the Spanish authorities under Article 4 of Regulation(EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that there is history of safe and significant consumption before 15 May 1997 of seeds of the plant species Pinus halepensis Mill. However, no relevant information was provided on the safe and significant consumption of green pinecones and bark in foods in the European Union before that'),
('POL-NF-13661', 'Heyndrickxia coagulans', 'Bacillus coagulans, Weizmannia coagulans', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Heyndrickxia coagulans in foods and food supplements. The request of the microorganism to be used only in food was submitted to the Swedish Competent Authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome, which indicates that the use in food is novel, is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en. The use of the microorganism in food supplements is considered not novel.'),
('POL-NF-17021', 'Callinectes sapidus', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Callinectes sapidus, commonly known as the blue crab.'),
('POL-NF-16381', 'S-adenosyl-L-methionine disulfate tosylate', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns S-adenosyl-L-methionine disulfate tosylate. A request was submitted to the Lithuanian competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-15582', 'Salvia apiana Jeps.', 'Ramona polystachya (Benth.) Greene', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Salvia apiana is commonly known as white sage, California white sage, or bee sage, is an evergreen perennial shrub native to Southern California and Baja California. It grows in coastal sage scrub and chaparral habitats.'),
('POL-NF-11541', 'Solidago virgaurea', null, null, '[{"part":"Herbal mixte tincture (alcoholic infusion)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herbal mixed tincture of Solidago virgaurea (alcoholic infusion). According to the conclusion reached by the Ministry of Agriculture of the Czech Republic, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, the herbal mixed tincture of Solidago vir'),
('POL-NF-15423', 'Mammea americana L.', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruitflesh and its juice (fruit without peel and seed)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruitflesh of Mammea americana L. M . americana belongs to the family of Clusiaceae.'),
('POL-NF-15462', 'Mucuna pruriens (L.) DC', null, null, '[{"part":"seeds and roots","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the seeds and the roots of the plant Mucuna pruriens (L.) DC'),
('POL-NF-15118', 'Corynebacterium flavescens', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the microbial culture of Corynebacterium flavescens'),
('POL-NF-11301', 'Crataegus monogyna', 'Crataegus apiifolia Medik., Mespilus apiifolia (Medik.) B.D.Jacks., Mespilus monogyna (Jacq.) All., Oxyacantha apiifolia, Oxyacantha monogyna, Crataegus oxyacantha Thuill.', 'EN: Common Hawthorn, Glastonbury Thorn', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Flowers and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruits, flowers and leaves of Crataegus monogyna Jacq.'),
('POL-NF-17461', 'Lathyrus sativus L.', null, null, '[{"part":"Starch-enriched fractionated grass pea (Lathyrus sativus L.) powder (SFGPP)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'This entry concerns starch-enriched fractionated grass pea ( Lathyrus sativus L.) powder (SFGPP). A request was submitted to the Spanish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 regarding the novel food status of starch-enriched fractionated grass pea (Lathyrus sativus L.) powder (SFGPP). It was concluded that it was not novel.'),
('POL-NF-16942', 'Gnetum africanum', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves of Gnetum africanum Welw.'),
('POL-NF-09562', 'Graesiella emersonii', 'Chlorella emersonii Shihira & R.W.Krauss 1965', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Graesiella emersonii (Shihira & R.W.Krauss) H.Nozaki & al. 1995'),
('POL-NF-15301', 'Chelidonium majus L', null, null, '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the aerial plant parts. Herbaceous perennial , lobed pinnate leaves, yellow 4-petaled flowers, orange latex in stems. Native from Europe, North Africa, Western Asia; naturalized in North America. Belongs to the family Papaveraceae.'),
('POL-NF-15242', 'Turkesterone', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of turkesterone regardless of whether is chemically synthesised or extracted from Ajuga turkestanika .'),
('POL-NF-16001', 'Cotinus coggygria Scop.', null, 'DE: Gewöhnlicher Perückenstrauch', '[{"part":"Bark, leaf, flower","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns bark, leaf, flower of Cotinus coggygria Scop. It belongs to the family of Anacardiaceae. For fisetin see the corresponding entry.'),
('POL-NF-11521', 'Lactose derived from whey with degraded riboflavin', null, null, '[{"part":"Lactose derived from whey with degraded riboflavin","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns l actose derived from whey with degraded riboflavin . According to the conclusion reached by the Irish competent authorities (Food Safety Authority of Ireland) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, lactose derived from whey with degraded rib'),
('POL-NF-16045', 'Vitex negundo Linn.', 'Lagundi', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Vitex negundo Linn., commonly known as Lagundi in the Philippines, is a 2–8 m tall aromatic shrub or small tree in the Lamiaceae family. The request was submitted to the French authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en#L'),
('POL-NF-15721', 'Phaseolus vulgaris', null, null, '[{"part":"Hydrolysed peptide extract of black bean (Phaseolus vulgaris Savi)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns hydrolysed peptide extract of black bean ( Phaseolus vulgaris Savi ). The latter was submitted to the Spanish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was considered novel food. The conclusion are published on the Commission''s webpage: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-00248', 'Cinnamomum verum', 'Cinnamomum zeylanicum J. Presl', null, '[{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the bark and leaves of Cinnamomum verum. It is a small evergreen tree belonging to the family Lauraceae.'),
('POL-NF-00251', 'Cistus x incanus', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Infusion from the aerial parts","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Cistus x incanus L. is a species belonging to the family of Cistaceae. Also, the entry concerns infusion made from the aerial parts (herbs) of the plant Cistus × incanus L. which was submitted to the German competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-00144', 'Arbutus unedo', 'Arbutus cassinifolia Steud.', 'Strawberry tree, Irish strawberry tree, Killarney strawberry tree (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berry, pseudocarp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits (berry, pseudocarp) of Arbutus unedo L.'),
('POL-NF-00146', 'Areca catechu', 'Areca catechu f. communis Becc.', 'Betel nuts, Gua, Supari', '[{"part":"Seeds (nut)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the nut, which is the seed of the fruit of the oriental palm Areca catechu L.'),
('POL-NF-00147', 'Aristotelia chilensis', null, 'Maqui', '[{"part":"Fruits (berry)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the berries of Aristotelia chilensis Stuntz. It is a small tree from the Eleocarpaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00254', 'Citrus junos', 'Citrus aurantium subsp. junos Makino', 'Yuzu, Yuja, Ichang-Zitrone, Ichandrins (DE)', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits of Citrus junos Siebold ex Tanaka. Citrus junos belongs to the plant family Rutaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00256', 'Clinoptilolite', null, 'Cleanolina, Vulkansand, Clinoptilolith (DE)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Clinoptilolite is a vulcanic sand.'),
('POL-NF-00257', 'Clitoria ternatea', null, 'EN: Butterfly pea, Asian pigeonwings', '[{"part":"Flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the flowers of Clitoria ternatea. It is a plant that belongs to the family of Fabaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00258', 'Cnicus benedictus', 'Centaurea benedicta (L.) L.', 'CZ: Benedikt lékařský', '[{"part":"Aerial parts, fruit, leaves and top","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the aerial parts, fruit, leaves and top of Cnicus benedictus L. It is a thistle-like plant in the family Compositae.'),
('POL-NF-00151', 'Artemisia vulgaris L.', null, 'EN: common mugwort, DE: Gemeine Beifuß, FR: armoise commune, DK:gråbynke, ES: artemisa, IT: artemisia comune, PT: artemísia-comum, NL:bijvoet, SE: gråbo, FI: pujo, EE: harilik puju, LT: paprastasis kietis,PL: bylica pospolita, BG: див пелин, CZ: pelyněk černobýl, LV: parastāvībotne, SI: navadni pelin, HU: fekete üröm', '[{"part":"Leaf, flowering tops, stem, rhizome","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Herb and aqueous extract of the aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herb, the use of the aqueous extract of the aerial parts, the leaf, flowering tops, stem, and rhizome of Artemisia vulgaris L .'),
('POL-NF-00152', 'Arthrospira platensis', 'Arthrospira jenneri var. platensis (Gomont) Guarrera & Kühnemann 0, Oscillatoria platensis (Gomont) Bourrelly 1970, Spirulina jenneri var. platensis Nordstedt 1884, Spirulina platensis (Gomont) Geitler 1925', 'Spirulina (DE) (SL) (PL) (FI) (CZ) (DK)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Arthrospira platensis Gomont 1892'),
