('POL-NF-00067', 'Abies pectinata', 'Abies alba Mill.', 'EN: European silver fir, Silver fir, Whitewood, NL: Gewone zilverspar, Grote spar, Zilverspar, FR: Sapin pectiné, Sapin blanc, Sapin argenté, FI: Saksanpihta, DE: Weiß-Tanne, Abies pectinata', '[{"part":"Bark, branch, needle, seed and resin","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Abies alba is a fir native to the mountains of Europe from the Pyrenees north to Normandy, east to the Alps and the Carpathians, and south to southern Italy and northern Serbia'),
('POL-NF-00068', 'Acacia arabica', 'Acacia nilotioca (L.) Delile', 'EN: Indian gum, Arabic tree, Babul, Egyptian thorn, Prickly acacia, Sant tree, Al-sant, FR: Acacia du Nil, DE: Arabische Akazie, Gummi-Akazie, FI: Akaasia, NL: Echte acacia, Gom-acacia', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Gum","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the information available (Belgian list of plants that are considered to be not novel for the use in food supplements) only the use of following plant parts is authorized: fruit, bark, gum . Acacia nilotica (gum arabic tree, babul, Egyptian thorn, Sant tree, Al-sant or prickly acacia; called thorn mimosa in Australia; lekkerruikpeul or scented thorn in South Africa) is a species of Acacia (wattle) native to Africa and the Indian subcontinent.'),
('POL-NF-00069', 'Acacia nilotica', 'Acacia arabica', 'NL: Echte acacia, Gom-acacia', '[{"part":"Bark, fruit and gum","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruit, bark and gum of Acacia nilotica (L.) Willd. ex Delile'),
('POL-NF-00070', 'Acacia rigidula', 'Blackbrush Acacia', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the plant Acacia rigidula Benth.'),
('POL-NF-00167', 'Auxenochlorella protothecoides', 'Chlorella protothecoides Krüger 1894, Palmellococcus protothecoides (Krüger) Chodat 1909, Auxenochlorella protothecoides var. galactophila Unknown authority 0, Chlorella protothecoides var. galactophila Shihira & R.W.Krauss 1965', 'DE: Chlorella', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Czech competent authorities (Ministry of agriculture of the Czech republic) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Auxenochlorella protothecoides (Krüger) Kalina & Puncochárova is considered not novel in food.'),
('POL-NF-00168', 'Auxenochlorella pyrenoidosa', 'Chlorella pyrenoidosa H.Chick 1903', 'DE: Chlorella', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Czech competent authorities (Ministry of agriculture of the Czech republic) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Auxenochlorella pyrenoidosa (H.Chick) Molinari & Calvo-Pérez is considered not novel in food.'),
('POL-NF-00169', 'Avena sativa L.', null, 'oat (EN)', '[{"part":"Oat shoots (oat grass)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Oat seeds/grains/kernels and fiber from the aerial parts including hull","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Oats fermented with Lactiplantibacillus plantarum in liquid or dry form","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the use of fiber from the aerial parts, including hulls (without kernels) of Avena sativa L.. The history of consumption in the EU was established. According to the conclusion reached by the Finnish food Authority, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of nov'),
('POL-NF-00170', 'Backhousia citriodora', null, 'lemon myrtle [EN]', '[{"part":"Shoots and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the young shoots and leaves of Backhousia citriodora F. Muell . . It is s a medium-sized shrub or tree.'),
('POL-NF-00171', 'Bacopa monnieri', 'Allocalyx microphylla Cordem.', 'Baby tears, brhami, dwarf bacopa, herb of grace (EN)', '[{"part":"Leaves, herbs, rhizomes and tops","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves, herbs, rhizomes and tops of the plant of Bacopa monnieri (L.) Wettst. . It is a plant belonging to the family Scrophulariacase.'),
('POL-NF-00173', 'Bactris gasipaes', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Stems and fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Bactris gasipaes is considered not novel in food supplements. According to the conclusion reached by the Spanish competent authorities in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, the stems and fruits of Bactris gasipaes Kunth are considered not novel in food .'),
('POL-NF-00073', 'Acacia verek', 'Acacia senegal', 'Arabische gom, FR: Gommier blanc, acacia Sénégal, DE: Verek-Akazie, Acacia verek, EN: Gum Acacia, Gum Arabic Tree, Gum Senegal Tree', '[{"part":"Gum","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the gum of Acacia verek Guill. & Perr.'),
