('POL-NF-00183', 'Betula alleghaniensis', null, 'EN: Yellow Birch', '[{"part":"Bark and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the bark and leaves of Betula alleghaniensis. It is a species of birch'),
('POL-NF-00184', 'Betula alnoides', 'Betula acuminata Wall.', 'Berk (NL)', '[{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns thee bark of Betula alnoides Buch.-Ham.. It belongs to Betulaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00185', 'Betula pendula', 'Betula alba', 'EN: Silver Birch', '[{"part":"Leaves, bark and bud","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Sap/juice","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves, bark and bud of Betula pendula. In addition sap/juice is considered not novel. It is a widespread European birch. The closely related Betula platyphylla in northern Asia and Betula szechuanica of central Asia are also treated as varieties of Silver Birch by some botanists, as B. pendula var. platyphylla and B. pendula var. szechuanica respectively.'),
('POL-NF-00186', 'Betula pubescens', null, 'FI: Hieskoivu', '[{"part":"Leaves, flowers, bark and bud","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Sap/juice","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves, flowers, bark and bud of Betula pubescens . In addition sap/juice is considered not novel. It is a species of birch.'),
