('POL-NF-00189', 'Paecilomyces variotii', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Biomass of Paecilomyces variotii. According to the conclusion reached by the Finnish Food Authority in response to the requests submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 ( https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en ) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Biomass of Paecilomyces variotii is considered novel in food .'),
('POL-NF-00191', 'Borago officinalis', null, 'EN: borage, DE: borretsch, FR: bourrache officinale, DK: almindelig hjulkrone, NL: bernagie, ES: borraja, PT: borragem, IT: borragine, SE: gurkört, FI: rohtopurasruoho, EE: harilik kurgirohi, LT: vaistinė agurklė, LV: ārstniecības gurķene, PL: ogórecznik lekarski, BG: пореч, CZ: brutnák lékařský, GR: μπουράντζα, RO: limba mielului, SI: boraga, HU: borágó', '[{"part":"Leaves, flowers, seeds and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The leaves, flowers, seeds and seed oil of Borago officinalis L. are considered not novel.'),
('POL-NF-00192', 'Borojoa patinoi', null, 'EN: Borojo', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit of Borojoa patinoi Cuatrec. It is a tropical forest tree that belongs to the Rubiaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00193', 'Borojoa sorbilis', 'Alibertia sorbilis Ducke', 'EN: Borojo', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit of Borojoa sorbilis (Ducke) Cuatrec.. It is a genus of flowering plants in the Rubiaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00194', 'Boswellia serrata', null, 'Frankincense, indischer Weihrauch (DE)', '[{"part":"Gum resin and boswellic acid extract","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the gum resin and boswellic acid extracts from the gum resin from Boswellia Serrata Roxb. ex Colebr. It is a plant belonging to the Burseraceae Family .'),
('POL-NF-00092', 'Agave sisalana', 'Agave amaniensis Trel. & Nowell', 'Agave rigida', '[{"part":"Fructose syrup","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Any food use other than fructose syrup","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fructose syrup of Agave sisalana Perrine. It belongs to the Agavaceae Family .'),
('POL-NF-00093', 'Agave tequilana', 'Agave angustifolia subsp. tequilana (F.A.C.Weber) Valenz.-Zap. & Nabhan', 'Blue Agave, tequila agave (EN)', '[{"part":"Syrup","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the syrup from Agave tequilana F.A.C.Weber'),
('POL-NF-00094', 'Agmatine (4-aminobutyl) guanidine sulfate', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Agmatine (4-aminobutyl) guanidine sulfate is the decarboxylation product of the amino acid arginine and is an intermediate in polyamine biosynthesis.'),
('POL-NF-00095', 'Ajuga reptans', 'Ajuga abnormis Rouy', 'EN: Carpet bugleweed, common bugleweed, blue bugle, bugleherb, bugleweed, carpetweed, common bugle', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Extract from cell cultures","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves and herbs (aerial parts) derived from flowers of Ajuga reptans L. In addition, the entry concerns the extract of Ajuga reptans from cell cultures.'),
('POL-NF-00097', 'Albatrellus ovinus', null, 'Sheep polypore (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruiting body","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruiting body of Albatrellus ovinus.'),
('POL-NF-00195', 'Bovine lactoferrin', null, null, '[{"part":"Bovine lactoferrine in food supplements","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Bovine lactoferrine in foods other than food supplements","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Bovine lactoferrin is a protein that occurs naturally in cow’s milk. Bovine lactoferrin is not considered as novel in food supplements. However, when it is intended to be used in foods other than food supplements it is novel. As a novel food, bovine lactoferrin has been included in the Union list of authorized novel foods (Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2017/2470) to be used as a food ingredient under specific conditions of use and specifications.'),
('POL-NF-00196', 'Brassica eruca', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'See Eruca sativa'),
('POL-NF-00197', 'Brassica juncea', null, 'Mustard greens, Indian mustard, Chinese mustard, Leaf mustard, Brown mustard (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds, leaves and stem","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves, seeds and stem of Brassica juncea .'),
('POL-NF-00198', 'Brassica nigra', null, 'Black mustard, brown mustard (EN)', '[{"part":"Seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Seeds and aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the seed oil, the seeds and the aerial parts of Brassica nigra W.D.J.Koch.'),
('POL-NF-00199', 'Brewer''s spent grain', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Brewer''s spent grain is mainly composed of fiber and protein fractions from the residues of malt from beer brewing process and only contains a minor amount of chaff. It is considered as not novel, whereas the chaff as an ingredient is considered as novel.'),
('POL-NF-00200', 'Brewer’s spent grain fiber (BSG-F) and brewer’s spent grain protein (BSG-P)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns brewer’s spent grain fiber (BSG-F) and brewer’s spent grain protein (BSG-P) . According to the conclusion reached by the Dutch Novel Food Unit of the Medicines Evaluation Board Agency, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 ( https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en ) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, brewer’s spent'),
('POL-NF-00098', 'Albizia julibrissin', null, 'Seidenbaumblueten (DE)', '[{"part":"Flowers","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of flowers and bark of Albizia julibrissin Durazz. A request related to the use of the flowers Albizia julibrissin Durazz was submitted to the Estonian authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established for the flowers. Therefore, flowers of Albizia julibrissin Durazz are considered novel foods. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food'),
('POL-NF-00099', 'Allium chinense', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Allium chinense is considered as novel food .'),
