('POL-NF-00206', 'Camelina sativa', null, 'Camilina oil', '[{"part":"Seeds and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Plant belonging to the Brassicaceae family. It is native to Eastern Europe and Southwest Asia, where wild weedy forms survive other weedy types have evolved and are found in cereal and flax crops. The developed crop form was widely grown across Europe until the 1950s. The seeds and the seed oil of Camelina sativa are known to be used in the EU as a food or food ingredient.'),
('POL-NF-00106', 'Aloe ferox', null, 'Cape Aloe (EN)', '[{"part":"Inner part of the leaves (Gel or mucilage or pulp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the inner part of the leaves of Aloe ferox Miller. it is an arborescent perennial shrub (belonging to the Liliaceae Family). Native to southern and eastern Africa, the parts of the plant used are the leaves from which a yellow bitter juice and a gel can be obtained.'),
