('POL-NF-00110', 'Alpinia galanga', 'Alpinia alba (Retz.) Roscoe', 'Galangal, grote galantwortel (NL)', '[{"part":"Rhizome","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the rhizome of Alpinia galanga (L.) Willd.'),
('POL-NF-00207', 'Camellia furfuracea', null, 'čajovník otrubičnatý (CZ)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"SUBJECT_TO_A_CONSULTATION_REQUEST"}]'::jsonb, 'Belongs to the Theaceae Family. A shrub or small tree, 2-3 m tall, native to Asia (China, Vietnam and Laos). The leaves are coriaceous. Some historical uses are as ornamental shrubs and/or as a source of tea and seed oils. A negative opinion on the substantial equivalence of this oil with olive oil ( Olea europae) has been issued by The NL (07/08/2003). Due to differences in the composition and unclear information on the levels of undesirable substances and because of the uncertainty about the p'),
('POL-NF-00208', 'Camelus dromedarius', null, 'Wielbład jednogarbny (mleko) (PL)', '[{"part":"Milk","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concern the use and handling of (Camel) milk, which are considered as not novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00209', 'Canarium ovatum Engl.', null, 'Pili nuts (EN)', '[{"part":"Dried nuts","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the dried nuts (pili nuts) of Canarium ovatum Engl.'),
