('POL-NF-00228', 'Centella asiatica', 'Hydrocotyle asiatica L.', 'Gotu Kola, asiatischer Wassernabel (DE)', '[{"part":"Stem, flowers and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Centella asiatica extract (standardised to 40 % triterpenes)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the stem, flowers and leaves of Centella asiatica (L.).Urb. It belongs to the family of Apiaceae. Centella asiatica extract (standardised to 40 % triterpenes) was subject to a request “Mixture of plant extracts and purified bioactive substances” under Article 4 to the Czech competent authority. It was considered novel food. The conclusion are published on the Commission''s webpage: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-00229', 'Centrophorus squamosus', null, 'Shark liver oil (EN)', '[{"part":"Shark liver oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'This entry concerns only the use of shark liver oil of Centrophorus squamosus. The deep sea shark Centrophorus squamosus belongs to the Squalidae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00230', 'Ceratonia siliqua', null, 'EN: Carob tree, St John''s-bread', '[{"part":"Fruit, gum, seed and pod","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the fruit, gum, seed and pod of Ceratonia siliqua L. The carob tree, Ceratonia siliqua , is a species of flowering evergreen shrub or tree in the pea family, Fabaceae , that is native to the Mediterranean region.'),
('POL-NF-00231', 'Cervus elaphus', null, 'Deer horn powder (EN)', '[{"part":"Antlers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the use of the antlers as “deer horn powder” Cervus elaphus . Deer horn powder is made of ground antlers of Cervus elaphus (family Cervidae ).'),
