('POL-NF-00133', 'Annona cherimola', 'Annona pubescens Salisb.', 'Cherimoya, Cremfrucht, cherimolia, cherimoyabaum, Chirimoya, Chirimoyabaum, Jamaika-Apfel (DE)', '[{"part":"Fruit (berry, pseudocarp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit (botanically berry, pseudocarp) of Annona cherimola Mill.'),
('POL-NF-00134', 'Annona muricata', 'Annona bonplandiana Kunth', 'Soursop, Brazilian pawpaw, prickly custard apple, Soursapi (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds, fruit peels, leaves and roots","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the seeds, fruit peels, leaves, roots and fruits of Annona muricata L.'),
('POL-NF-00135', 'Annona reticulata', 'Annona excelsa Kunth', 'Annoona (FI)', '[{"part":"Fruit (berry, pseudocarp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit (berry, pseudocarp) of Annona reticulata L.'),
('POL-NF-00232', 'Cetraria islandica', null, 'Iceland Moss (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns all plant parts of Cetraria islandica (L.) Acharius s.l. Iceland moss belongs to the family of Parmeliaceae. Like all lichens, Cetraria islandica is made up of two types of plants, a fungus and an alga. The body (thallus) of the lichen is made up of the filaments, or hyphae, of the fungus and the plants live together in a mutually beneficial relationship known as symbiosis: the green alga synthesizes or makes food for itself and the fungus while the fungus absorbs and retains '),
('POL-NF-00233', 'Chamaemelum nobile', 'Anthemis nobilis L., Anacyclus aureus L., Anthemis aurea, Anacyclus nobilis', 'Chuven (BG)', '[{"part":"Inflorescence and flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the inflorescence and flowers of Chamaemelum nobile (L.) All. It is a low perennial plant found in dry fields and around gardens and cultivated grounds. It belongs to the plant family Asteraceae ( Compositae ).'),
('POL-NF-00234', 'Chenopodium album L.', null, 'EN: white goosefoot, DE: weiße gänsefuß, FR: chénopode blanc, DK: hvidmelet gåsefod, NL: melganzenvoet, PL: komosa biała, ES: cenizo, IT: farinello comune, PT: ansarina-branca, FI: jauhosavikka, SE: svinmålla, EE: valge hanemalts, LT: baltoji balanda, CZ: merlík bílý, SI: bela metlika, HU: fehér libatop', '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves of Chenopodium album L..'),
('POL-NF-00236', 'Chenopodium quinoa', null, 'Quinoa (PT)(DE) (ES) (DK)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seeds of Chenopodium quinoa. It belongs to the Amaranthaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00237', 'Chioca', null, 'Oca', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'This vegetable originated from the Andes of South America. It ranges from pale creamy-white to deep purlish red in colour and sweet to slightly astringent in taste, depending on variety. It is a popular root crop of the Andes together with potato. It is easy to prepare, as it does not require peeling, however, as it is a root crop, proper cleaning is essential before roasting, steaming or frying.'),
('POL-NF-00136', 'Annona squamosa', 'Annona asiatica L.', 'Søtannona (NO)', '[{"part":"Fruit (berry, pseudocarp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruit (berry, pseudocarp) of Annona squamosa L.'),
('POL-NF-00137', 'Antennaria dioica', 'Antennaria dioica var. australis Gris', 'Mountain everlasting (EN)', '[{"part":"Flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the flowers of Antennaria dioica (L.) Gaertn.'),
('POL-NF-00139', 'Aphanizomenon flosaquae var. flosaquae', null, 'Alga Klamath, Super Blue Green, Bluegreen, AFA (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Aphanizomenon flos-aquae va r. flos-aquae. This cyanobacterium belonging to the genus Aphanizomenon is a variety of the species Aphanizomenon flos-aquae .'),
('POL-NF-00140', 'Apis mellifera', null, 'hunajamehiläinen (FI)', '[{"part":"Bee venom","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the use of bee venom in food.'),
('POL-NF-00141', 'Apricot Kernel (Prunus Armeniaca L.)', null, null, '[{"part":"Apricot Kernel Drink and Fermented Apricot Kernel Cream","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns Apricot Kernel Drink and Fermented Apricot Kernel Cream (Prunus armeniaca L.) . According to the conclusion reached by the Austrian competent authorities (Austrian Agency for Health and Food Safety) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status,'),
('POL-NF-00238', 'Chlamydomonas reinhardtii', null, null, '[{"part":"The dried biomass powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Chlamydomonas reinhardtii dried biomass powder. A consultation request was submitted to the competent authorities of Ireland under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, Chlamydomonas reinhardtii dried biomass powder is considered a novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00240', 'Chlorella pyrenoidosa', 'Chlorella vulgaris, Auxenochlorella pyrenoidosa', 'Chlorella (DE)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Chlorella pyrenoidosa is a specie of freshwater green microalga in the division Chlorophyta.'),
('POL-NF-00241', 'Chlorella sorokiniana', null, 'Chlorella (DE) (DK)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Czech competent authorities (Ministry of agriculture of the Czech republic) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Chlorella sorokiniana is considered not novel in food.'),
('POL-NF-00242', 'Chlorella vulgaris', 'Chlorella pyrenoidosa var. duplex (Kützing) West null Pleurococcusbeijerinckii Artari 1892, Chlorella communis Artari 1906, Chlorellavulgaris var. viridis Chodat 1913, Chlorella terricola Gollerbach[Hollerbach] 1936, Chlorella candida Shihira & R.W.Krauss 1965', 'Chlorella (DE) (DK)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Czech competent authorities (Ministry of agriculture of the Czech republic) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Chlorella vulgaris is considered not novel in food.'),
('POL-NF-00243', 'Chondrus crispus', 'Polymorpha crispa (Stackhouse) Stackhouse 1809, Fucus ceranoides var.lacerus (Linnaeus) Lightfoot 1777, Fucus lacerus Linnaeus 1763, Fucus crispus Linnaeus 1767, Fucus norvegicus Gunnerus 1772, Fucus crispusvar. aequalis Goodenough & Woodward 1797, Fucus patens Goodenough & Woodward 1797, Fucus crispus var. brunneus Goodenough & Woodward 1797, Fucus crispus var. virens Goodenough & Woodward 1797, Fucus lacerus Stackhouse 1797, Fucus crispus var. filiformis Goodenough & Woodward 1797, Fucus crispus var. sarniensis Turner 1802, Fucus crispus var. planus Turner 1802, Fucus crispus var. lacerus Turner1802, Fucus crispus var. patens (Goodenough & Woodward) Turner1802, Fucus polymorphus J.V.Lamouroux 1803, Polymorpha norvegicus (Gunnerus) Stackhouse 1809, Gigartina heterocarpa (Postels & Ruprecht) D.H.Kim 1976', 'Irish moss (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the whole plant of Chrondus crispus . It is a species of red algae which grows abundantly along the rocky parts of the Atlantic coast of Europe and North America'),
('POL-NF-00244', 'Chrysanthellum americanum', 'Anthemis Americana Mutis ex L.', null, '[{"part":"Leaves and aerials parts with flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves and aerials parts with flowers of Chrysanthellum americanum (L.) Vatke. It is a plant belonging to the family of Compositae .'),
('POL-NF-00647', 'Resveratrol', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Resveratrol derived from Japanese knotweed ( Fallopia japonica / Polygonum cuspidatum ) with a content of more than 98% trans-resveratrol.'),
('POL-NF-00648', 'Rhamnogalacturonan-rich pectin hydrolysate', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Rhamnogalacturonan-rich pectin hydrolysate is derived from carrot pomace ( Daucus carota subsp. Sativus ). According to the conclusion reached by Ireland competent authorities in response to a request under Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en), this product is considered novel food'),
('POL-NF-00649', 'Rhaponticum carthamoides (Willd.) Iljin', 'Leuzea carthamoides (Willd.) DC.', 'Stemmacantha carthamoides', '[{"part":"Roots and herb","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the roots and herb of Rhaponticum carthamoides. Rhaponticum carthamoides belongs to the plant family Asteraceae.'),
('POL-NF-00650', 'Rheum rhabarbarum L.', null, 'EN: rhubarb, DE: rhabarber, FR: rhubarbe, DK: rabarber, NL: rabarber, ES: ruibarbo, PT: ruibarbo, SE: rabarber, FI: raparperi, EE: kurdlehine rabarber, PL: rabarbar kędzierzawy, BG: вълнообразният ревен, CZ: reveň kadeřavá, GR: ραβέντι, HU: rebarbara', '[{"part":"Stem","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Root and rhizome","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns diferent parts of Rheum rhabarbarum L'),
('POL-NF-00651', 'Rhodiola Rosea', null, 'Golden root (EN)', '[{"part":"Root and herb","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the root and herb of the Rhodiola rosea L. plant. Rhodiola rosea belongs to the plant family Crassulaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00653', 'Ribose', null, 'D-Ribose (DE)', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'D-ribose is a five-carbon sugar (pentose with the molecular formula C5H10O5 and the CAS No. 50-69-1) chemically related to other 5 carbon sugars, such as arabinose and xylose and found primarily in ribonucleic acid and in all living cells. Ribose and its related compound, deoxyribose, are the building blocks of the backbone chains in nucleic acids, better known as DNA and RNA.'),
('POL-NF-00347', 'Euterpe edulis', 'Euterpe edulis var. clausa Mattos', null, '[{"part":"Fruits (botanically berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Euterpe spp.'),
('POL-NF-00348', 'Euterpe spp.', null, 'Mart, Assai palm, Acai palm, pinapalm (NL)', '[{"part":"Fruits (botanically berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruit (berries) from Euterpe oleracea Mart. and Euterpe edulis Mart. Both belong to the Arecaceae (Palmae) family.'),
('POL-NF-00349', 'Eutrema japonicum', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Wasabia japonica'),
('POL-NF-00350', 'Evodia lepta', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of leaves of Evodia lepta Merr. A request was submitted to the Estonian authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, the leaves of Evodia lepta are considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en'),
('POL-NF-00353', 'Fallopia japonica', null, 'EN: Japanese knotweed, DE: japanische staudenknöterich, FR: renouée du Japon, DK: japanpileurt, ES: hierba nudosa japonesa, IT: poligono del Giappone, NL: japanse duizendknoop, FI: japanintatar, SE: parkslide, PL: rdestowiec ostrokończysty, BG: японската фалопия, CZ: křídlatka japonská, LV: japānas dižsūrene, LT: japoninis pelėvirkštis, SK: pohánkovec japonský, SI: japonski dresnik, HU: ártéri japánkeserűfű', '[{"part":"Aerial parts, flowers, leaves, roots, shoot, stems and seed of plant","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts, flowers, leaves, roots, shoot, stems and seed of plant from Fallopia japonica'),
