('POL-NF-00662', 'Rozites caperatus', 'Cortinarius caperatus', 'Gypsy mushroom (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Rozites caperatus mushroom. Rozites caperatus (or Cortinarius caperatus ), commonly known as the gypsy mushroom, is a highly esteemed edible mushroom of the genus Cortinarius found in northern regions of Europe and North America.'),
('POL-NF-00664', 'Rubus chamaemorus', null, 'Cloudberry (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the berry of Rubus chamaemorus L. It belongs to the plant family Rosaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00665', 'Rubus glaucus Benth.', null, 'Andean raspberry, mora de castilla (EN); ostružiník (CZ)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit of Rubus glaucus . Rubus glaucus belongs to the plant family Rosaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00362', 'Foeniculum vulgare', null, 'Fennel (EN)', '[{"part":"Leaves (petiole), fruits (schizocarp) and shoots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Fennel ( Foeniculum vulgare Mill. ) is a plant species in the genus Foeniculum (treated as the sole species in the genus by most botanists). It is a member of the family Apiaceae (formerly Umbelliferae ). It is a hardy, perennial, umbelliferous herb, with yellow flowers and feathery leaves. It is generally considered indigenous to the shores of the Mediterranean, but has become widely naturalised elsewhere.'),
('POL-NF-00363', 'Fragaria x ananassa (Duchesne ex Weston) Duchesne ex Rozier', null, 'Fragaria x ananassa, Garden strawberry (EN), Havejordbær (DK), Gartenerdbeere (DE), Fraise (FR), Morango (PT), Fresa (ES), Fragola (IT), Jordgubbe (SE), Aardbei (NL), Poziomka truskawka (PL), Puutarhamansikka (FI), Dārza zemene (LV), Braškė (LT), Aedmaasikas (EE), Градинската ягода (BG), Jahodník velkoplodý (CZ), Φράουλα (GR)', '[{"part":"Infusion of the leaves and fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the infusion of the leaves and the fruits from Fragaria x ananassa (Duchesne ex Weston).'),
