('POL-NF-00666', 'Rubus suavissimus', 'Rubus chingii var. suavissimus (S.K.Lee) L.T.Lu', 'Chinese blackberry (EN)', '[{"part":"Non-concentrated aqueous infusion","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves and fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns tea, herbal and fruit infusions containing or prepared with leaves of Rubus suavissimus and intended to be consumed as such. It also concerns the use of Rubus suavissimus leaves and fruits in food supplements. It belongs to the plant family Rosaceae . The aqueous infusion is made with water only and has not been subject to any selective extraction. The use is only limited to : - Tea, herbal and fruits infusions consumed as such ; - Non-alcoholic flavoured drinks based on herba'),
