('POL-NF-00571', 'Passiflora edulis', 'Passiflora cuneifolia Cav.', 'Maracuyá común, fruto de la pasión, Fruta de la pasión (ES)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit of Passiflora edulis Sims.'),
('POL-NF-00572', 'Paullinia cupana', 'Paullinia brasiliensis Lodd. ex Radlk.', 'Guaranà (IT)', '[{"part":"Fruits and seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruits and seeds of Paullinia cupana Kunth'),
('POL-NF-00573', 'Pisum sativum', 'Lathyrus oleraceus Lam.', null, '[{"part":"Protein hydrolysates","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"High purity protein concentrate","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Vegetable protein concentrate derived from Pisum sativum sprouts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the protein hydrolysates obtained by the mild acid hydrolysis of Pisum sativum L. . According to the conclusion reached by the Irish Food Safety Authority in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, pea protein hydrolysate is not novel . The entry'),
('POL-NF-00673', 'Russula paludosa', null, 'Tall russula (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Russula paludosa mushroom. Russula paludosa belongs to the mushroom family Russulaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00674', 'Russula vinosa', 'Russula obscura', 'Darkening Brittlegill (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Russula vinosa mushroom. Russula vinosa belongs to the mushroom family Russulaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00675', 'Rutin', null, 'Rutoside', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Rutin, which is a bioflavonoid found in many plants.'),
('POL-NF-00676', 'Saba senegalensis (A.DC.) Pichon.', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Saba senegalensis , is a fruit producing plant of the Apocynaceae family, native to the Sahel region of sub-Saharan Africa'),
('POL-NF-00677', 'Saccharina latissima', 'Ulva latissima Linnaeus 1753, Ulva lactuca var. latissima (Linnaeus) A.P.De Candolle 1805, Phycoseris latissima (Linnaeus) Fraudenfeld 1854, Fucus saccharinus Linnaeus 1753, Ulva latissima Gunnerus 1766, Ulva maxima Gunnerus 1776, Ulva longissima Gunnerus 1776, Ulva fusca Hudson 1778, Laminaria saccharina (Linnaeus) J.V.Lamouroux 1813', 'DE: Zuckertang, Zuckerkombu', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Saccharina latissima (Linnaeus) C.E.Lane, C.Mayes, Druehl & G.W.Saunders 2006.'),
('POL-NF-00678', 'Saccharomyces cerevisiae', null, null, '[{"part":"Yeast protein","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Dried yeast fermentate","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Iron-enriched yeast","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns Saccharomyces cerevisiae protein, dried yeast fermentate produced by Saccharomyces cerevisiae and Iron-enriched S accharomyces cerevisiae. The yeast protein and its components are normally consumed through yeast and yeast extracts present in food, it is obtained by a conventional physical and enzymatic process. According to the conclusion reached by the Irish competent authority (FSAI), in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implement'),
('POL-NF-00679', 'Salacia reticulata', null, null, '[{"part":"Roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the root of Salacia reticulata Wight in food supplements. Salacia reticulata Wight is a large woody climbing shrub native to Sri Lanka and Southern regions of India.'),
('POL-NF-00377', 'Germinated hemp seed produced by malting', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the use of germinated hemp seed (Cannabis sativa L.) produced by malting. According to the conclusion reached by the Finnish competent authorities (Finnish Food Authority) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, germinated hemp seed (Cannabi'),
('POL-NF-00379', 'Gigantochloa levis', 'Bambusa levis', 'Grönsaksbambu (SE)', '[{"part":"Steam (botanically immature shoots)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the stem (botanically immature shoot) of Gigantochloa levis (Blanco) Merr. Gigantochloa levis (Blanco) Merr. is one of the edible bamboo species. Gigantochloa is a tropical genus of giant clumping bamboo, similar to the genus Bambusa . It belongs to the plant family Poaceae (Gramineae) and is found in Southeast Asia.'),
('POL-NF-00380', 'Ginkgo biloba', null, 'dvokrpi ginkovec (SL)', '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the leaves of Ginkgo biloba L. Ginkgo biloba belongs to the Ginkgoaceae family and is native to the south-east of China.'),
('POL-NF-00381', 'Glebionis coronaria L.', null, 'EN: garland chrysanthemum, FR: chrysanthème couronné, DK: kronokseøje, NL: gekroonde ganzenbloem, ES: ojo de buey, IT: crisantemo incoronato, BG: ядливата хризантема, SE: kranskrag', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts of Glebionis coronaria L..'),
('POL-NF-00479', 'Lithothamnion calcareum', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Lithothamnion calcareum (Pallas) J.E.Areschoug 1852'),
('POL-NF-00480', 'Lucuma obovata', 'Lucuma obovata Kunth', 'Lucuma (DE)', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruit of Lucuma bifera Molina. It belongs to the Sapotaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00481', 'Lupinus albus', null, 'White lupin, Egyptian lupin (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the seeds of Lupinus albus L..'),
('POL-NF-00482', 'Lupinus angustifolius', null, 'Blue lupin (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seed of Lupinus angustifolius L.. Lupinus species ((i.e.Lupinus albus L., Lupinus angustifolius L. Lupinus luteus L.) contain quinolizidine alkaloids (QA), which are notoriously bitter and toxic to both humans and farm animal. Lupin seeds with a high concentration of QAs need to be debittered before consumption.'),
('POL-NF-00483', 'Lupinus luteus', null, 'Yellow Lupin (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seed of Lupinus luteus L.. Lupinus species ((i.e.Lupinus albus L., Lupinus angustifolius L. Lupinus luteus L.) contain quinolizidine alkaloids (QA), which are notoriously bitter and toxic to both humans and farm animal. Lupin seeds with a high concentration of QAs need to be debittered before consumption.'),
('POL-NF-00574', 'Pelargonium sidoides', null, null, '[{"part":"Root","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the powdered root of Pelargonium sidoides DC.. According to the conclusion reached by the German competent authority in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, powdered root of Pelargonium sidoides DC. is considered novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00575', 'Penicillium oxalicum var. armeniaca', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Penicillium oxalicum var. armeniaca.'),
('POL-NF-00576', 'Gadus macrocephalus', null, null, '[{"part":"Peptide extract from hydrolysed parts","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns peptide extract from hydrolysed parts of pacific cod (Gadus macrocephalus). According to the conclusion reached by the German competent authority in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, peptide extract from hydrolysed parts of pacific cod'),
('POL-NF-00578', 'Perilla frutescens', 'Melissa cretica [Soland.], Ocimum frutescens L., Perilla frutescens var. laviniata W.Mill. & L.H.Bailey', 'perilla (PT) (LV) (ES)', '[{"part":"Herb and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the herbs and seeds oil of Perilla frutescens (L.) Britton.'),
('POL-NF-00580', 'Persea americana', 'Persea americana var. americana', 'EN: Avocado, Avocado pear, alligator pear', '[{"part":"Oil from the fruit flesh","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns avocado oil that is produced from the fruit flesh of Persea americana Mill..'),
('POL-NF-00680', 'Salicornia europea', 'Salicornia annua Sm.', 'Marsh samphire (EN)', '[{"part":"herbs","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herbs of Salicornia europea L. It belongs to the Amaranthaceae Family is a well known annual halophyte.'),
('POL-NF-00682', 'Salvia miltiorrhiza', null, 'CZ: Čínská šalvěj', '[{"part":"Leaf, root and its alcoholic extract","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaf, root, and alcoholic root extract from Salvia miltiorrhiza Bunge in food supplements. Salvia miltiorrhiza (Tan Shen, Chinese sage, Red-rooted sage) is a shade-growing perennial flowering plant in the genus Salvia .'),
('POL-NF-00683', 'Sanguisorba minor', 'Poterium sanguisorba L.', 'EN: salad burnet, DE: kleine wiesenknopf, FR: pimprenelle, DK: bibernelle, NL: kleine pimpernel, ES: pimpinela major, FI: pikkuluppio, SE: pimpinell, PL: krwiściąg mniejszy, CZ: krvavec menší, EE: harilik mustnupp, GR: σαγκουισόρβον το έλασσον, SI: mala strašnica, HU: kis vérfű', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Root","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts and roots of Sanguisorba minor Scop.'),
('POL-NF-00684', 'Satureja hortensis L.', null, 'PL: Cząber ogrodowy', '[{"part":"Leaves and shoots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the leaves, shoots and aerial parts of Satureja hortensis L..'),
('POL-NF-00685', 'Schinus terebinthifolius', null, 'EN: Brazilian pepper, Aroeira, Florida holly, Rose Pepper, Christmasberry', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruit of Schinus terebinthifolius.'),
('POL-NF-00383', 'Glucomannan (Konjac mannan)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Glucomannan obtained from the konjac root (Amorphophallus konjac) is considered not novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00384', 'Glucosamine sulphate', null, 'siarczan glukozaminy (PL)', '[{"part":"Glucosamine Sulphate","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of glucosamine sulphate.'),
('POL-NF-00385', 'Gossypium sp.', null, 'Cotton, Sea island cotton, Levant cotton, Upland cotton (EN)', '[{"part":"Oil obtained from seed (capsule) of Gossypium barbadese L., Gossypium herbaceum L. and Gossypium hirsutum L.","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Seeds of Gossypium herbaceum L. and Gossypium hirsutum L.","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of oil obtained from seed (capsule) of Gossypium barbadese L. ., Gossypium herbaceum L. and Gossypium hirsutum L. and seeds of Gossypium herbaceum L . and Gossypium hirsutum L. Gossypium species belong to the Malvaceae Family. It is cultivated in warm arid climates and requires deep soil. Cottonseeds contain gossypol, a naturally occurring pigment protecting the plant. This polyphenolic compound is of toxicological concern.'),
('POL-NF-00386', 'Gracilaria verrucosa', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Gracilaria verrucosa (Hudson). It is a red alga widely distributed in seaside areas of many countries'),
('POL-NF-00387', 'Gracilariopsis longissima', 'Fucus longissimus S.G.Gmelin 1768, Ceramium longissimum (S.G.Gmelin) Roth 1800, Fucus verrucosus Hudson 1762, Fucus confervoides Linnaeus 1763, Ceramium confervoides F.H.Wiggers 1780, Sphaerococcus confervoides (F.H.Wiggers) Stackhouse 1797, Flagellaria verrucosa (Hudson) Stackhouse 1809, Gigartina confervoides (Linnaeus) J.V.Lamouroux 1813, Sphaerococcus verrucosus (Hudson) C.Agardh 1817, Sphaerococcus confervoides var. verrucosus (Hudson) C.Agardh 1822, Gracilaria confervoides (Linnaeus) Greville 1830, Hypnea confervoides (C.Agardh) J.Agardh 1842, Gracilaria verrucosa (Hudson) Papenfuss 1950, Gracilariopsis verrucosa (Hudson) Steentoft, L.M.Irvine & Farnham 1995', 'DE: Ogo, Ogo-nori', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Gracilariopsis longissima (S.G.Gmelin) Steentoft, L.M.Irvine & Farnham 1995.'),
('POL-NF-00388', 'Griffonia simplicifolia', 'Bandeiraea simplicifolia (Vahl ex DC.) Benth; Schotia simplicifolia Vahl ex DC.', null, '[{"part":"Seeds and extracts of Griffonia simplicifolia seeds up to maximum 30% of 5-HTP","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the seeds of Griffonia simplicifolia (Vahl ex DC.) Baill., and the extracts of Griffonia simplicifolia seeds which contain up to maximum 30% 5-HTP. Other extracts from Griffonia simplicifolia seeds are considered as novel food. See entry 5-hydroxytryptophan'),
('POL-NF-00485', 'Lycium barbarum', 'Lycium barbarum Mill.', 'Matrimony vine (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the berries of Lycium barbarum L. It is a Chinese plant belonging to the Solanaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00486', 'Lycopene', null, 'likopen (PL)', '[{"part":"Substance/extract/preparation","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Synthetic lycopene","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Lycopene from Blakeslea trispora","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Lycopene from tomatoes (Lycopersicon esculantum L.)","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Lycopene oleoresin from tomatoes (Lycopersicon esculantum Mill.)","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns lycopene from different sources. It is a red, fat-soluble pigment. This carotenoid is found in certain plants and microorganisms. Lycopene from different sources including red tomatoes is authorised as a food additive (colour). Lycopene from tomatoes is also known to be used in food supplements but from other sources (synthetic lycopene, Lycopene from Blakeslea trispora, Lycopene from tomatoes ( Lycopersicon esculantum L .) and Lycopene oleoresin from tomate ( Lycopersicon esc'),
('POL-NF-00487', 'Macadamia integrifolia', null, 'Macadamia (DE) (ES)', '[{"part":"Nuts and oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the nuts and oil of Macadamia integrifolia Maiden & Betche. Macadamias belong to the Proteaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00488', 'Macrodiscus lactiflorus', 'Distictis lactiflora', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Distictis lactiflora and Amphilophium lactiflorum (Vahl) L.G.Lohmann'),
('POL-NF-00489', 'Malpighia glabra', 'Malpighia punicifolia L.', 'Acerola, Barbados cherry tree (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the berries of Malpighia glabra L .. The edible part of Malpighia glabra is the fruit (botanically berry).'),
('POL-NF-00581', 'Persea gratissima', 'Persea americana Mill.', null, '[{"part":"Oil from the fruit flesh","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Persea americana Mill.'),
('POL-NF-00583', 'Phalaris canariensis', 'Phalaris aquatica Delile ex Boiss.', 'EN: Canary grass', '[{"part":"Grain","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the grain of Phalaris canariensis L. It belongs to the family Poaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00584', 'Pharbitis hederecea', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Ipomoea hederacea L.'),
('POL-NF-00585', 'Phaseolus angularis', 'Vigna angularis (Willd.) Ohwi & H.Ohashi', 'Adzuki, Red bean (EN)', '[{"part":"Beans","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the beans of Phaseolus angularis (Willd.) W.Wight. It belongs to the Fabaceae Family. This species should not be confused with the well-known "common bean" ( Phaseolus vulgaris ).'),
('POL-NF-00586', 'Phaseolus coccineus', 'Lipusa formosa (Kunth) Alef.', 'SE: Rosenböna', '[{"part":"Seeds (derived from the pod)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the use of seeds (derived from the pod) of Phaseolus coccineus L..'),
('POL-NF-00587', 'Phaseolus cylindricus', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Vigna unguiculata'),
('POL-NF-00279', 'Cortinarius caperatus', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Rozites caperatus'),
('POL-NF-00280', 'Corylus avellana', null, 'Common hazel (EN)', '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the leaves of Corylus avellana L.. It belongs to the Betulaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00282', 'Coutarea latiflora', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Coutarea latiflora DC. in food supplements. It belongs to the plant family Rubiaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00283', 'Crambe maritima L.', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"All other plant parts including fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Crambe maritima L.'),
('POL-NF-00284', 'Crataegus laevigata', 'Crataegus laevigata subsp. laevigata', 'Chinese hawthorn (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits, flowers and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruits, flowers and leaves of Crataegus laevigata (Poir.) DC. It is a species belonging to the Rosaceae Family'),
('POL-NF-00389', 'Grifola frondosa', null, 'Maitake (DE)', '[{"part":"Dehydrated mycelium powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Fruiting body and aqueous extract powder","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruit bodies and dehydrated mycelium powder of Grifola frondosa. A request was submitted to the Finish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 regarding the novel food status of extract powder from the fruiting body of Grifola frondosa. It was concluded that it was not novel. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en.'),
('POL-NF-00391', 'Gypsophila struthium', null, 'Egyptian soapwort root (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"SUBJECT_TO_A_CONSULTATION_REQUEST"}]'::jsonb, 'Perennial plant belonging to the Caryophyllaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00392', 'Hamamelis virginiana', null, 'NL: Virginische toverhazelaar', '[{"part":"Leaves and bark/rind","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of leaves and bark/rind of Hamamelis virginiana L..'),
('POL-NF-00393', 'Harpagophytum procumbens', null, 'Devil´s Claw (EN)', '[{"part":"Roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the use of the root of Harpagophytum procumbens (Burch.) DC. ex Meisn. Harpagophytum procumbens (Burch.) DC. ex Meisn belongs to the Pedaliaceae Family and is a native of Southern Africa.'),
('POL-NF-00394', 'Helichrysum italicum', null, 'EN: curry plant, DE: italienische strohblume, FR: immortelle d’Italie, DK: karryplante, NL: kerrieplant, ES: curry, IT: elicriso italiano, PT: erva-do-caril, HU: olasz szalmagyopár, GR: Ελίχρυσος', '[{"part":"Aerial parts, leaves, flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts, leaves and flowers of Helichrysum italicum (Roth) G. Don (Gnaphaliuum italicum Roth ).'),
('POL-NF-00395', 'Helix aspersa maxima', null, 'Gros-gris (FR)', '[{"part":"Meat and the eggs","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the meat and the eggs of the snail Helix aspersa maxima.'),
('POL-NF-00490', 'Malpighia punicifolia', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruits (berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Malpighia glabra'),
('POL-NF-00491', 'Malus communis', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Buds, flowers, leaves and roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruits, bud, flowers, leaves and roots of Malus communis subsp. sylvestris (L.) Gams . See Malus sylvestris'),
('POL-NF-00492', 'Malus sylvestris', null, 'EN: Crab apple, European wild apple, Wild crab apple', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Buds, flowers, leaves and roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits, bud, flowers, leaves and roots of Malus sylvestris (L.) Mill.'),
('POL-NF-00494', 'Manihot esculenta', 'Manihot utilissima Pohl', 'Maniok jedlý (CZ)', '[{"part":"Roots and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the roots and the leaves of Manihot esculenta Crantz . It belongs to the family Euphorbiaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00495', 'Manihot utilissima', null, null, '[{"part":"Roots and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'See Manihot esculenta Crantz'),
('POL-NF-00588', 'Phellodendron chinense', 'Phellodendron chinense var. chinense', null, '[{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the bark of Phellodendron chinensis C.K.Schneid. The request was submitted to the Estonian authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, the bark of Phellodendron chinensis is considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en under the entry Chrysanthemum morif'),
('POL-NF-00589', 'Phlebodium aureum', 'Chrysopteris aurea Link', 'Polypodium leucotomos, Polypodium aureum, Polypodium aureum', '[{"part":"Summits, rhizomaes","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the summits and rhizomaes of Phlebodium aureum J.Sm. It belongs to the plant family Polypodiaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00590', 'Phyllantus emblica', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Emblica officinalis'),
('POL-NF-00591', 'Phyllostachys edulis', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Phyllostachys pubescens'),
