('POL-NF-00595', 'Picea abies', 'Abies abies Druce', 'EN: Norway spruce', '[{"part":"Young shoots (sprouts)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves (needles), flowers, pine cones and resin","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the young shoots (sprouts), leaves (needles), flowers, pine cones and resin of Picea abies (L.) H.Karst.'),
('POL-NF-00596', 'Pinitol', null, 'D-Pinitol, pinitol (PL) (CZ) (SL)', '[{"part":"substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'D-pinitol (2-0-Methyl-1,2,4 cis-3,5,6 trans hexahydroxy-cyclohexane) is derived from pine trees. Chemically, it is defined as an as 0-methyl-inositol.'),
('POL-NF-00597', 'Pinus balsamea', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Abies balsamea'),
('POL-NF-00598', 'Pinus koraiensis', 'Apinus koraiensis (Siebold & Zucc.) Moldenke', 'Korean Pine (EN)', '[{"part":"Seed and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the nuts and oil of Pinus koraiensis Siebold & Zucc. In the EU the use of nuts and oil from Pinus koraiensis as food or fodd ingredient is established. However, preparations with free fatty acids from the oil have no history of consumption in the EU.'),
('POL-NF-00599', 'Pinus pinaster', 'Pinus corteana hort. ex Beissn.', 'French maratime pine, tree bark (EN)', '[{"part":"Bark and bud","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the bark and bud of Pinus pinaster Aiton'),
('POL-NF-00600', 'Pinus sibirica', 'Abies sibirica Ledeb.', 'Siberian pine, Sibirian cedar (EN)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the nuts of Pinus sibirica (Ledeb.) Turcz. It belongs to the Pinaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00292', 'Curcumin', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the use of curcumin, an extract complex from the root of Curcuma longa L. According to the conclusion reached by the Swedish competent authorities (Swedish Food Agency) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status. Curcumin is novel. The status in'),
('POL-NF-00293', 'Curcuminoids', null, null, '[{"part":"Extract","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the turmeric extract of the rhizome of Curcuma longa L, containing up to 95% of curcuminoids (also referred to as curcumins). The main constituents are curcumin and, to a lesser extent, demethoxycurcumin and bisdemethoxycurcumin, in the proportion naturally occurring in C. longa. A history of consumption in the EU has been demonstrated for such an extract in food supplements. Any process that enhance the solubility or bioavailability might however be subject to the novel foo'),
('POL-NF-00294', 'Cyclopia sp.', null, 'Heuningbos (AFR)', '[{"part":"Wood (shrub) and herb","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the wood (shrub) and herb of Cyclopia sp .These shrubs belong to the genus Cyclopia and the plant family Fabaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00295', 'Cyperus esculentus', null, 'Yellow Nutsedge, Earth almond (EN)', '[{"part":"Tubers (roots)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Tuber oil","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the tubers (roots) and tuber oil of Cyperus esculentus . It belongs to the family Cyperaceae. According to the conclusion reached by the Spanish competent authorities (Spanish Agency for food safety and nutrition) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel fo'),
('POL-NF-00297', 'D-mannose', null, 'D-mannosa (CZ)', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'D-Mannose is a simple sugar, the 2-epimer of glucose, that occurs naturally in some plants, including cranberries'),
('POL-NF-00298', 'Dacryodes edulis', null, 'FR: Safoutier, prunier, atanga', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit of Dacryodes edulis.'),
('POL-NF-00299', 'Daucus carota L.', null, 'Peen, wortel (NL)', '[{"part":"Roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the roots of Daucus carota L. (carrot). It belongs to the Apiaceae (Umbelliferae) family.'),
('POL-NF-00403', 'Himanthalia elongata', 'Fucus elongatus Linnaeus 1753', 'Sea thong, hongweed, Buttonweed, Sea Haricots, Sea Spaghetti (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Himanthalia elongata (Linnaeus) S.F.Gray 1821. It is a brown alga, which is found in the Baltic Sea, the North Sea and the north east Atlantic Ocean.'),
('POL-NF-00404', 'Hippophae rhamnoides', 'Argussiera rhamnoides (L.) Bubani, Elaeagnus rhamnoides (L.) A.Nelson, Hippophaes rhamnoideum (L.) St.-Lag.,Rhamnoides hippophae Moench, Osyris rhamnoides (L.) Scop.,', 'Seabuckthorne, Sea buckthorn (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berries), leaves and flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Seeds and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits (berries), leaves, flowers, seeds and seed oil of Hippophae rhamnoides L. It belongs to the Elaeagnaceae family .'),
('POL-NF-00405', 'Hirneola polytricha', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Auricularia polytricha'),
('POL-NF-00406', 'Sargassum fusiforme (Harvey) Setchell 1931', 'Cystophyllum fusiforme Harvey 1860, Turbinaria fusiformis (Harvey) Yendo1907, Hizikia fusiformis (Harvey) Okamura 1932, Cystophyllum fusiformevar. clavigerum Harvey 1860', 'Hijiki, Hiziki (DE)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Sargassum fusiforme (Harvey) Setchell 1931'),
('POL-NF-00407', 'Honckenya peploides L.', null, 'EN: sea sandwort, DE: salzmiere, FR: pourpier de mer, DK: strandarve, NL: zeepostelein, ES: arenaria de mar, FI: suola-arho, EE: merihumur, LT: sultingoji jūrasmiltė, SE: saltarv, PL: honkenia', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts of Honchenya peploides L. Ehrh. (Arenaria peploides L.).'),
('POL-NF-00408', 'Hoodia gordonii', 'Hoodia albispina N.E.Br.', 'Hoodia cactus, hoodia (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Hoodia gordonii (Masson) Sweet ex Decne.'),
('POL-NF-00503', 'Methylsulfonylmethane', null, 'matylsulfonylmetan (CZ)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Methylsulfonylmethane is a naturally occurring organosulfur compound with the formula (CH₃)₂SO₂.'),
('POL-NF-00504', 'methylliberine', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'IUPAC name: 2-Methoxy-1,7,9-trimethylpurine-6,8-dione.'),
('POL-NF-00505', 'Micronized and microencapsulated ferric diphosphate', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns micronized and microencapsulated ferric diphosphate intended to be used as an ingredient in food supplements. The request was submitted to the Czech authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that micronized and microencapsulated ferric diphosphate should be considered not novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00506', 'Mineral enriched fungal biomass (Aspergillus oryzae)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Mineral enriched fungal biomass ( Aspergillus oryzae ). According to the conclusion reached by the Food Safety Authority of Ireland (FSAI) in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 ( https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en ) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Mineral enriched fungal biomass ( Aspergillus oryzae ) is co'),
('POL-NF-00507', 'Momordica charantia', 'Cucumis argyi H.Lév.', 'Bitter gourd, balsam pear, balsam apple (EN)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the berries and leaves of Momordica charantia L. It belongs to the Cucurbitaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00508', 'Momordica grosvenorii', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Siraitia grosvenorii'),
('POL-NF-00601', 'Pinus sylvestris', 'Pinus borealis Salisb.', 'EN: Scots Pine', '[{"part":"Pine cone syrup, preserved pine cones, and needle extract","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Cones, needles, bud, bark and young shoots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the needle extract, cones, needles, bud, bark and young shoots of Pinus sylvestris L. This species belongs to the plant family Pinaceae. Two requests concerning pine cone syrup and preserved pine cones were submitted to the German competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en'),
('POL-NF-00602', 'Piper nigrum', 'Muldera multinervis Miq.', 'EN: Black pepper, white pepper', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruit of Piper nigrum L. (black pepper).'),
('POL-NF-00603', 'Pistacia lentiscus', null, null, '[{"part":"Oil from berries","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the oil from berries of Pistacia lentiscus L. A request was submitted to the Italian authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was established. Therefore, oil obtained from Pistacia lentiscus berries is not considered a novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en under the entry Pistacia lentiscus'),
('POL-NF-00605', 'Plantago afra', 'Psyllium afrum (L.) Mirb., Plantago afra var. parviflora (Desf.) Lewalle, Plantago cynops L., Plantago parviflora Desf., Plantago pseudopsyllium Desf.', null, '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seeds of Plantago afra L.'),
