('POL-NF-00513', 'Monascus major', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'See Monascus purpureus'),
('POL-NF-00514', 'Monascus purpureus', 'Monascus anka, Monascus araneosus, Monascus major, Monascus rubiginosus, Monascus vini', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Red Yeast Rice Powder RYR-SWM352 (Monascus purpureus)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the so-called ''red yeast fermented rice'' in food supplements and red yeast rice powder RYR-SWM352 (Monascus purpureus). Red yeast rice is produced by fermentation of a yeast on rice. The yeast on this entry is Monascus purpureus Went. Depending on the yeast strain used and the conditions of fermentation, the yeast can enrich the rice with substances known as monacolins, including monacolin K. A request was submitted to the Italian competent authority under Article 4 of Regulat'),
('POL-NF-00515', 'Monascus rubiginosus', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Monascus purpureus'),
('POL-NF-00516', 'Monascus vini', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Monascus purpureus'),
('POL-NF-00608', 'Plantago maritima', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Common names EN: sea plantain, DE: strand-wegerich, FR: plantain maritime, DK: strandvejbred, NL: zeeweegbree, ES: llantén marítimo, IT: piantaggine delle argille, SE: gulkämpar, FI: meriratamo, EE: rand-teeleht, LI: strandjwaegbrei, PL: babka nadmorska, CZ: jitrocel přímořský, HU: sziki útifű The leaves of Plantago maritima L. are considered as not novel.'),
('POL-NF-00609', 'Plantago ovata', 'Plantago brunnea E.Morris, Plantago ispaghula Roxb.', 'Psyllium-fröska, Loppfröskal, babka jajowata (PL)', '[{"part":"Seeds and seed husks","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seeds and their husks of Plantago ovata Forssk. It belongs to the Plantaginaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00611', 'Pleurotus eryngii (dehydrated mycelium powder)', null, null, '[{"part":"Dehydrated mycelium powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Pleurotus eryngii dehydrated mycelium powder. The request was submitted to the Spanish authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, Pleurotus eryngii dehydrated mycelium powder is considered a novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en under the entry Pleurotus er'),
('POL-NF-00612', 'Pleurotus ostreatus', null, 'EN: Oyster mushroom', '[{"part":"Beta-glucan and fruiting body","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Mycelium and dehydrated mycelium powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruiting body, beta glucan and mycelium of Pleurotus ostreatus L . According to the conclusion reached by the Spanish agency for food safety and nutrition (AESAN) in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Pleurotus ostreatus mycelium and d'),
('POL-NF-00306', 'Desmodium gangeticum', null, 'Asumat, salparni, orila, konicz (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Desmodium gangeticum (L.) DC.'),
('POL-NF-00307', 'Desugared fermented orange juice', null, null, '[{"part":"Desugared fermented orange juice","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Desugared fermented orange juice results from the fermentation of orange juice with a yeast that is commonly used in food processing, which reduces the sugar content of the orange juice while producing ethanol that is subsequently removed by evaporation.According to the conclusion reached by the Directorate General for Food and Veterinary of Portugal, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/s'),
('POL-NF-00308', 'DHA and EPA ethyl esters oil from Schizochytrium sp.', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns DHA and EPA ethyl esters oil from Schizochytrium sp. Schizochytrium sp. are often referred to as microalgae for practical or functional reasons. However, they belong to the net slime moulds (Labyrinthulomycetes) and are considered fungus-like organisms. According to the conclusion reached by the Food Safety Authority of Ireland (FSAI) in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food'),
('POL-NF-00309', 'Dioscorea alata', 'Dioscorea alata var. globosa (Roxb.) Prain', 'Yam (NL)', '[{"part":"Roots (tuber)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the use of the roots (tuber) of Dioscorea alata L. (Ube) .Yam is the common name for some species in the genus Dioscorea (family Dioscoreaceae). These are perennial herbaceous vines cultivated for the consumption of their starchy tubers in Africa, Asia, Latin America and Oceania. A request was submitted to the Italian competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 regarding the novel food status of powder from Dioscorea alata L. (Ube) tubers. It was conc'),
