('POL-NF-00633', 'Pseudotsuga menziesii', null, 'EN: douglas fir, DE: gewöhnliche douglasie, FR: sapin de douglas, DK: douglasgran, NL: douglasspar, ES: abeto de Douglas, IT: abete di douglas, PT: abeto-de-douglas, SE: douglasgran, FI: lännendouglaskuusi, EE: harilik ebatsuuga, LT: didžioji pocūgė, PL: daglezja zielona, CZ: douglaska tisolistá, RO: duglas, SK: duglaska tisolistá, SI: duglazija, HU: amerikai duglászfenyő', '[{"part":"Needles and shoots","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the needles and shoots of Pseudotsuga menziesii (Mirb) Franco.'),
('POL-NF-00634', 'Psidium guineense', null, 'IT: Guava della Guinea', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruits (botanically berry) of Psidium guineense Sw. Psidium guineense is also used as natural source for flavourings. Guavas are plants in the myrtle family (Myrtaceae) genus Psidium (meaning "pomegranate" in Latin)'),
('POL-NF-00635', 'Ptychopetalum olacoides', null, 'Muira puama (PT) (ES)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the Ptychopetalum olacoides obtained from potency wood. Shrub or small tree up to 5 m in height and native from the Brazilian Amazon and other parts of northern Brazil. The small white flowers have a pungent fragrance similar to jasmine.'),
('POL-NF-00636', 'Pueraria montana var. lobata', 'Pueraria lobata (Willd.) Ohwi', 'Kudzu (EN, ES, PT, LV, NL, FR)', '[{"part":"Starch of the root","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Alcohol extract of kudzu root","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Aqueous extracts flowers, leaves and roots of kudzu","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the roots, leaves and the flowers of Pueraria montana var. lobata (Willd.) Maesen & S.M.Almeida ex Sanjappa & Predeep. The starch from the root of Pueraria lobata is not novel in foods. Alcohol extracts made from Pueraria lobata requires authorisation under Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 on novel foods. However, extracts made from those plants parts may fall under the Novel Food Regulation. Pueraria lobata is a species of plant in the botanical family Fabaceae (Leguminosae). At lea'),
('POL-NF-00637', 'Pueraria mirifica', null, 'kwao kreu', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns Pueraria mirifica Airy Shaw & Suvat. It is a plant belonging to the Leguminosae Family and native to Thailand where it is also known as white kwao kreu.'),
('POL-NF-00638', 'Pueraria thunbergiana', null, 'Kudzu', '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'See Pueraria lobata .'),
('POL-NF-00639', 'Punica granatum L.', 'Punica florida Salisb.', 'ES: Granada', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Pericarp, flower, seed","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Seed oil","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Pomegranate extract with 40 % punicalagin","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit, pericarp, flower, seed and seed oil of the Punica granatum L . (Pomegranate). The pomegranate ( Punica granatum ) is a fruit-bearing deciduous shrub or small tree growing to between five and eight metres tall. It belongs to the plant family Punicaceae. According to the conclusion reached by the French competent authorities (DGCCRF) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.e'),
('POL-NF-00335', 'Epimedium sagittatum', 'Aceranthus macrophyllus Blume ex K.Koch, Aceranthus sagittatus Siebold & Zucc., Aceranthus triphyllus K.Koch, Epimedium coactum var. longtouhum H.R.Liang, Epimedium ikariso Siebold ex Regel, Epimedium sagittatum var. glabratum T.S.Ying, Epimedium sagittatum var. oblongifoliolatum Z.Cheng, Epimedium sagittatum var. sagittatum, Epimedium sagittifolius Farrer, Epimedium sinense Siebold ex Miq.', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns all plant parts of Epimedium sagittatum. It belongs to the family Berberidaceae'),
('POL-NF-00336', 'Equisetum arvense', 'Field Horsetail', 'Field Horsetail, Common Horsetail (EN)', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only the use of aerial parts of Equisetum arvense L. It is a herbaceous perennial plant, which belongs to the plant family Equisetaceae.The use of the aerial parts of Equisetum arvense L. is known in food supplements and as an ingredient in tea.'),
('POL-NF-00337', 'Eragrostis tef', 'Cynodon abyssinicus (Jacq.) Raspail', 'teff, lovegrass', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of seeds of Eragrostis tef (Zuccagni) Trotter.'),
('POL-NF-00339', 'Eruca sativa', null, 'Eruca, ervafedorenta, rábanosilvestre, rúcula (PT)', '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of leaves from Eruca sativa (L.) Mill. It belongs to the Brassicaceae (Cruciferae) family.'),
('POL-NF-00440', 'L-alpha glycerylfosforylcholine', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the substance L-alpha glycerylfosforylcholine (L-alpha-GPC) in food and food supplements. According to the conclusion reached by the Czech competent authorities in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, L-alpha glycerylfosforylcholine'),
('POL-NF-00441', 'L-citrulline malate', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns L-citrulline malate.'),
('POL-NF-00442', 'L-fucose', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance/extract/preparation","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns L-fucose.'),
('POL-NF-00443', 'L-Theanine', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance/extract/preparation","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Substance/extract/preparation","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'L-Theanine extracted and isolated from green tea ( Camellia sinensis ) is not novel only in food supplements. L-Theanine from other sources is novel food Also, the entry concerns L-theanine produced by fermentation with Escherichia coli which was submitted to the Italian competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-00445', 'Lactarius deliciosus', null, 'Edelreizker, Echter Reizker (DE)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Lactarius deliciosus. It belongs to the plant family Russulaceae.'),
