('POL-NF-00643', 'Raphanus sativus', null, 'EN: radish, DE: garten-rettich, FR: radis, DK: radise, NL: tuinradijs, ES: rábano, IT: ravanello comune, PT: rabanete, SE: rädisa, FI: retiisi, EE: redis, PL: rzodkiewT: valgomasis ridikas, RO: ridiche, SK: red’kev siata, SI: redkvica, HU: retek zwyczajna, BG: репичката, CZ: ředkev setá, GR: ρεπάνι, LV: dārza redīsi, L', '[{"part":"seed capsules/siliques and roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Flowers and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns different parts of Raphanus sativus L.'),
('POL-NF-00644', 'Rauwolfia vomitoria', null, 'African serpentwood (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns all plant parts of Rauwolfia vomitoria. Rauwolfia vomitoria belongs to the plant family Apocynaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00645', 'Red clay sea salt', null, 'EN: Alaea salt, Hawaiian red salt', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the red clay sea salt product. It is an unrefined sea salt that has been mixed with iron oxide rich volcanic clay called ‘alaea’, which gives the seasoning salt its characteristic brick red color.'),
