('POL-NF-00757', 'Trigonella foenum-graecum', 'Buceras foenum-graecum (L.)', 'EN: Fenugreek, sicklefruit', '[{"part":"seeds (pod)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Only the seeds of Trigonella foenum-graecum (fenugreek) have been used as food within the EU before 15 May 1997. Fenugreek ( Trigonella foenum-graecum ) is a plant in the family Fabaceae (Leguminosae, subfam. Papilionoideae). It is indigenous to countries on the eastern shores of the Mediterranean and cultivated in India, Egypt and Africa. The cuboid yellow to amber coloured fenugreek seeds are frequently used in the preparation of pickles, curry powders, and pastes, and the spice is often encou'),
('POL-NF-00759', 'Triticum aestivum', 'Cardamindum majus Moench', 'Wheat (EN)', '[{"part":"seeds, bran, germ oil, fiber from stem, juice from young shoots of wheatgrass just before the jointing stage","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Wheat bran extract","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Fermented (fermentation with baker’s yeast) wheat germ extract","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns seeds, bran, germ oil, fiber from stem, juice from young shoots and aerial parts of Triticum aestivum L. It also concerns the Triticum aestivum bran extract and fermented Triticum aestivum germ extract According to the conclusion reached by the Finnish food Authority, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps '),
('POL-NF-00760', 'Tropaeolum majus L.', null, 'EN: garden nasturtium, DE: große kapuzinerkresse, FR: grande capucine, DK: tallerkensmækker/blomsterkarse, NL: oost-indische kers, ES: capuchina, IT: nasturzio, PT: cinco-chagas, SE: indiankrasse, FI: isoköynnöskrassi, PL: nasturcja większa, CZ: lichořeřišnice větší, EE: suur mungalill, LT: didžioji nasturtė, RO: condurul-doamnei, SK: kapucínka väčšia, SI: velika kapucinka, HU: kerti sarkantyúka', '[{"part":"Herb","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial part with flowers, fruits, seeds,","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herb, aerial parts, fruits and seeds of Tropaeolum majus L. Aerial part with flowers, fruits, seeds , of Tropaeolum majus L. are considered as not novel in food supplements.'),
