('POL-NF-00779', 'Viola tricolor', 'Jacea tricolor (L.) Opiz', 'EN: wild pansy, DE: wilde stiefmütterchen, FR: pensée sauvage, DK: stedmoderblomst, NL: driekleurig viooltje, ES: pensamiento salvaje, IT: viola del pensiero, PT: amor-perfeito, SE: styvmorsviol, FI: keto-orvokki, EE: aaskannike, LT: trispalvė našlaitė, SK: fialka trojfarebná, PL: fiołek trójbarwny, CZ: violka trojbarevná, BG: трицветната теменуга, RO: panseluța de camp, HU: háromszínű árvácska', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts of Viola tricolor L.'),
('POL-NF-00780', 'Viscum album', 'Viscum album var. Album', 'FR: Gui', '[{"part":"Leaves and Stem","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Infusion of the aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of leaves and stem of Viscum album L.. In addition, herbal infusions or tea prepared with the aerial parts of Viscum album L. are considered as not novel.'),
('POL-NF-00781', 'Vitellaria paradoxa', null, null, '[{"part":"shea butter","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Polyphenol-rich extract","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Vitellaria paradoxa C.F.Gaertn., commonly known as shea tree, is a tree of the family Sapotaceae . The request concerns the use of shea butter which is a fat that is extracted from the nuts of the shea tree. This product is not novel. In addition, a request concerning polyphenol-rich extract derived from Vitellaria paradoxa . C.F. Gaertn. was submitted to the Italian competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link'),
('POL-NF-00784', 'Wasabia japonica', 'Eutrema japonicum (Miq.) Koidz', null, '[{"part":"Root","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the root of Wasabia japonica (Miq.) Matsum. It is a plant of the family Brassicaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00785', 'Whey treated with UV radiation', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns whey treated with UV radiation. According to the conclusion reached by the Italian competent authorities (Italian Ministry of Health. Directorate General for Hygiene, Food Safety and Nutrition) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Whey'),
('POL-NF-00686', 'Schisandra chinensis', 'Kadsura chinensis Turcz, Maximowiczia amurensis Rupr., Maximowiczia chinensis (Turcz.) Rupr., Maximowiczia japonica (A.Gray) K.Koch, Schisandra chinensis var. leucocarpa P.H.Huang & L.H.Zhuo, Schisandra nigra f. viridicarpa (Y.N.Lee) M.Kim, Schisandra japonica (Siebold. & Zucc. ex A. Gray) Hance., Sphaerostema japonicum A.Gray', 'Cytryniec chiński (PL)', '[{"part":"Fruits (berries)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Young (boiled) leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruits and young leaves of Schisandra sinensis (Turcz.) Baill. Schizandra chinensis belongs to the plant family Schizandraceae . It is a creeping plant with small red berries native to Northern China.'),
