('POL-NF-00711', 'Spent coffee grounds, defatted spent coffee grounds and defatted unused coffee grounds', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the use of spent coffee grounds, defatted spent coffee grounds and defatted unused coffee grounds (from Coffea sp., mainly Coffea arabica L. and Coffea canephora (Robusta)). According to the conclusion reached by the Danish competent authorities (Danish Veterinary and Food Administration) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on '),
('POL-NF-00712', 'Sphaerotrichia divaricata', null, 'sferotrichia (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the brown algae Sphaerotrichia divaricata (C.Agardh) Kylin 1940. It belongs to the Chordariaceae Family'),
('POL-NF-00713', 'Sphingolipids', null, 'sfingolipidy (PL)', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Sphingolipids are a class of lipids derived from the aliphatic amino alcohol sphingosine. The sphingosine backbone is O-linked to a charged head group such as ethanolamine, serine or choline. The backbone is also amide-linked to an acyl group, such as a fatty acid. Sphingolipids are often found in neural tissue and play an important role in both signal transmission and cell recognition.'),
('POL-NF-00715', 'Spleen peptides', null, 'Spleen Factors, Spleen Peptides, Spleen Polypeptides, (immune) Transfer Factors, Spleen Oligo- and Polypeptides, , Hydrolyzed/Predigested Spleen Extract, Facteurs Spléniques (FR), Extrait de Rate (Hydrolysé) (FR), Extrait Splénique (Prédigéré) (FR), Extrait Splénique (FR)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns bovine or porcine spleen peptides.'),
('POL-NF-00716', 'Splenopentin', null, 'splenopentyna (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Splenopentin (SP-5, Arg-Lys-Glu-Val-Tyr) is a synthetic peptide corresponding to the region 32-34 of the splenic hormone called splenin.'),
('POL-NF-00717', 'Spondias lutea', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruits (botanically drupe)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Spondias mombin L.'),
('POL-NF-00718', 'Spondias mombin', 'Spondias lutea L.', null, '[{"part":"Fruits (botanically drupe)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Spondias lutea L.'),
('POL-NF-00719', 'Spondias purpurea', 'Spondias cirouella Tussac', 'PT: Mombim', '[{"part":"Fruits (botanically drupe)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruits ((botanically drupe) of Spondias purpurea L. It is a genus of flowering plants in the cashew family, Anacardiaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00720', 'Stachyose', null, 'stachioza (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Stachyose is a soluble alfa-galactoside.'),
