('POL-NF-00743', 'Theobroma grandiflorum', 'Bubroma grandiflorum Willd. ex Spreng.', 'Großblütiger Kakao (DE)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Pulpe (fruit preparations)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Seeds/kernels","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits of Theobroma grandiflorum (Willd. ex Spreng.) K.Schum. It belongs to the Sterculiaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-00747', 'Thysostachys regia', 'Thyrsostachys siamensis Gamble', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Thyrsostachys siamensis'),
('POL-NF-00744', 'Thermopsis lanceolata', null, 'EN : False Lupine, bush pea', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the information available to Member States'' competent authorities, this product was not consumed in the EU to a significant degree as a food before 15 May 1997. Thermopsis lanceolata is considered novel in food. Therefore, a pre-market authorisation in accordance with Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 is required before it can be placed as food on the EU market.'),
('POL-NF-00745', 'Thymopentin', null, 'tümopentiin (ET)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Thymopentin, also known as TP-5, is a peptide of five amino acids (Arg-Lys-Asp-Val-Tyr). It is a synthesized derivative of thymopoietin, a naturally occurring hormone produced by the thymus gland. Thymopentin has the CAS No 69558-55-0 and has the molecular formula: C30H49N9O9 H-Arg-Lys-Asp-Val-Tyr-OH.'),
('POL-NF-00746', 'Thyrsostachys siamensis', 'Bambusa regia Thomson ex Munro, Bambusa siamensis Kurz ex Munro, Thyrsostachys regia (Munro) Bennet', 'Bambus rozlogowy (PL)', '[{"part":"Stem","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the stem (botanically immature shoot) of Thyrsostachys siamensis and belongs to the plant family Poaceae (Gramineae).'),
('POL-NF-00748', 'Tinospora cordifolia', null, null, '[{"part":"Non-concentrated aqueous infusion","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of tea liked beverage from Tinospora cordifolia'),
('POL-NF-00749', 'Torula yeast (Cyberlindnera jadinii) biomass', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Torula yeast (Cyberlindnera jadinii). The request was submitted to the Irish authorities (FSAI) under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that, Torula yeast (Cyberlindnera jadinii) is not novel when used as a food ingredient.'),
('POL-NF-00750', 'Tragopogon porrifolius', 'Tragopogon porrifolius f. porrifolius', 'EN: Salsify, oyster plant, vegetable oyster', '[{"part":"Root","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of roots of Tragopogon porrifolius . It belongs to the plant family Asteraceae (Compositae).'),
('POL-NF-00268', 'Colocasia esculenta', 'Colocasia antiquorum f. acuatica Makino', 'Þerrirót, Karabískt spínat (IS)', '[{"part":"Roots (rhizome) and leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the roots (rhizome) and leaves of Colocasia esculenta (L) Schott. It belongs to the Araceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00289', 'Crepidula fornicata', null, 'American Limpet (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"SUBJECT_TO_A_CONSULTATION_REQUEST"}]'::jsonb, 'Crepidula fornicata is a species of hermaphrodite mollusc which can tolerate a wide range of environmental conditions and are well developed in wave-protected areas such as bays, estuaries or sheltered sides of wave-exposed islands.'),
('POL-NF-00249', 'Cinnamomum zeylanicum', null, 'Echter Zimt, Ceylonzimt (DE)', '[{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of bark and leaves of Cinnamomum zeylanicum .'),
('POL-NF-09541', 'Gelidium corneum', 'Fucus corneus Hudson 1762, Sphaerococcus corneus (Hudson) Stackhouse 1797, Nereidea cornea (Hudson) Stackhouse 1816, Gigartina cornea (Hudson) S.F.Gray 1821, Delesseria cornea (Hudson) Greville 1828, Fucus corneus var. sesquipedalis Clemente 1807', 'De: Agar', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Gelidium corneum (Hudson) J.V.Lamouroux 1813'),
('POL-NF-00105', 'Aloe barbadensis', 'Aloe chinensis BAK, aloe ferox Mill.', null, '[{"part":"Inner part of the leaves (Gel or mucilage or pulp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Aloe ferox'),
('POL-NF-00255', 'Citrus × mitis Blanco', 'Citrus × microcarpa Bunge, ×Citrofortunella microcarpa (Bunge) Wijnands', 'Calamondin, Calamansi or Kalamansi', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits of Citrus × mitis Blanco. It belongs to the plant family Rutaceae and is a hybrid between two well-known citrus fruits: Mandarin ( Citrus reticulata ) and oval Kumquat ( Citrus japonica )'),
('POL-NF-00071', 'Acacia senegal', 'Senegalia senegal (L.) Britton', 'NL: Arabische gom', '[{"part":"Gum","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the gum of Acacia senegal (L.) Willd.'),
('POL-NF-00064', 'Abelmoschus esculentus', 'Hibiscus esculentus L.', 'Okra (EN, FI, DK, NL, FR, IS, NO, PL, ES, DE, SE)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits (botanically immature capsules) of Abelmoschus esculentus Moench. It is an annual herbaceous shrub belonging to the Malvaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-09561', 'Gracilaria gracilis', 'Fucus gracilis Stackhouse 1801, Fucus confervoides var. gracilis(Stackhouse) Turner 1802, Flagellaria gracilis (Stackhouse) Stackhouse1809, Gigartina confervoides var. gracilis (Stackhouse) S.F.Gray 1821,Sphaerococcus confervoides var. gracilis (Stackhouse) C.Agardh 1822,Gracilaria confervoides f. gracilis (Stackhouse) Grunow 1874,Gracilaria confervoides var. gracilis (Stackhouse) Batters 1902, Fucusalbidus Esper 1800, Fucus procerrimus Esper 1800, Gracilariaconfervoides var. procerrima (Esper) Greville 1830, Fucus gulamanM.Blanco 1837, Sphaerococcus capillaris Kützing 1863, Gracilaria confervoides var. capillaris Sonder 1880, Gracilaria confervoides f.tenuissima Rosenvinge 1931, Gracilaria verrucosa var. procerrima(Esper) M.P.Reis 1981', 'DE: Ceylon Moss', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Gracilaria gracilis (Stackhouse) Steentoft, L.M.Irvine & Farnham 1995'),
('POL-NF-00290', 'Crocodylus nilotikus', null, 'Nīlas krokodils (LV)', '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'The marketing in the Community of this species is subject to the provision of the Council Regulation EC n° 338/97 of the 9th December 1996 on the protection of species of wild fauna and flora. Crocodylus nilotikus is listed in Annex A and B of the above Regulation in compliance with the objectives, principles and provisions of the Convention on International Trade in Endangered Species of wild fauna and flora (CITES).'),
('POL-NF-11185', 'Scenedesmus sp.', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns a number of algal species ( Scenedesmus acutus Meyen 1829, Scenedesmus quadricauda (Turpin) Brébisson 1835, Desmodesmus subspicatus (Chodat) E.Hegewald & A.W.F.Schmidt 2000, Desmodesmus communis (E.Hegewald) E.Hegewald 2000, Tetradesmus almeriensis Turiel, Garrido-Cardenas, Gómez-Serrano, Acién, Carretero-Paulet & S.Blanco 2021, Tetradesmus dimorphus (Turpin) M.J.Wynne 2016, Tetradesmus obliquus (Turpin) M.J.Wynne 2016), which are part of a request submitted to the Czech compe'),
('POL-NF-00190', 'Bixa orellana', null, 'annatto (SE)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Bixa orellana L.. is is a tree belonging to the Bixaceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-05961', 'Bambusa spp.', 'Bamboo (EN) (PT)', null, '[{"part":"Shoots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves and shoots of Bambusa spp. It belongs to the grass family grass Poaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00065', 'Abies alba', 'Abies pectinata (Lam.) DC.', 'NL: Gewone zilverspar, Grote spar, Zilverspar', '[{"part":"Extracts of any of the following parts: bark, branch, needle, seed and resin","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the extracts of the following parts (bark, branch, needle, seed and resin) of Abies alba Mill.'),
('POL-NF-00235', 'Chenopodium pallidicaule', 'Chenopodium canihua', 'merlik bledy (CZ)', '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the seeds of Chenopodium pallidicaule. It is an Andean cereal with a high nutritional value, containing twice as much protein as foods such as wheat, rice and oats. It is native of the Peruvian Altiplano and is produced mainly in the Puno region to the north of Lake Titicaca.'),
('POL-NF-00246', 'Chrysanthemum morifolium', null, null, '[{"part":"Other parts","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Flower and alcohol extracts of the flower","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the flower (and its alcohol extracts) and other parts of Chrysanthemum morifolium Ramat.'),
('POL-NF-09440', 'Lacticaseibacillus casei', 'Lactobacillus casei, Lactobacillus zeae', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Lacticaseibacillus casei bacteria . These bacteria have been used as characteristic ingredients in fermentation of food products'),
('POL-NF-06022', 'Lama glama', null, 'Lama (NL, FR, DE, EN)', '[{"part":"Meat and milk","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the milk and meat of Lama glama , which is a mammalia belonging to the Camelidae. There is a history of consumption of the meat and milk of lama in the United Kingdom before 15 May 1997. Therefore, the meat and milk is not considered as a novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00402', 'Hieracium pilosella', 'Pilosella officinarum Vaill.', 'mouse-ear hawkweed', '[{"part":"Herbs and Roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Herbal tincture (alcoholic infusion)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herbs and roots of Hieracium pilosella L. It is a yellow-flowered species of Asteraceae, native to Europe and northern Asia. Additionally, according to the conclusion reached by the Ministry of Agriculture of the Czech Republic, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for dete'),
('POL-NF-08621', 'Hoodia parviflora N.E.Br.', null, null, '[{"part":"Dried aerial parts","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the dried aerial parts of Hoodia parviflora N.E.Br.'),
('POL-NF-06061', 'Dimorphandra mollis', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Quercetin (≥ 95%)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Dimorphandra mollis Benth, a tree species in the genus of Dimorphandra and quercetin extracted from the plant. Quercetin (≥ 95%)obtained by extraction of Dimorphandra mollis Benth. was subject to a consultation request to the German competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en under the entry ‘Q’'),
('POL-NF-00250', 'Cistanche deserticola', null, 'cistanche (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns the use of Cistanche deserticola Y.C.Ma plant. It is a Chinese perennial fleshy herbaceous plant, which belongs to Orobanchaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-10622', 'Streptococcus salivarius', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns only Streptococcus salivarius strains K12 and M18'),
('POL-NF-00338', 'Eriobotrya japonica', 'Crataegus bibas Lour.', 'Japaninmispeli (FI)', '[{"part":"Fruit (pome), leaf, seed","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the fruit (pome), leaf and seed from Eriobotrya japonica (Thunb.) Lindl. It is an evergreen large shrub or small tree, with a rounded crown, short trunk and woolly new twigs that belongs to the plant family Rosaceae ( Malaceae ).'),
('POL-NF-15104', 'Acetobacter aceti', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns microbial cultures of Acetobacter aceti'),
('POL-NF-00369', 'Fulvic acid', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Fulvic acid is an organic acid that is isolated from humus (organic fraction of soil). Fulvic acid is considered as novel food.'),
('POL-NF-15109', 'Bifidobacterium thermophilum', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the microbial culture of Bifidobacterium thermophilum'),
('POL-NF-00334', 'Epimedium macranthum', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Epimedium grandiflorum'),
('POL-NF-10621', 'Yarrowia lipolytica', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole (as a characteristic ingredient)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Yarrowia lipolytica yeast biomass, chromium-containing yeast (Yarrowia lipolytica) biomass and selenium-containing yeast (Yarrowia lipolytica) biomass.","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Yarrowia lipolytica. These yeasts have been used as characteristic ingredients in fermentation of food products. It also concerns the use of Yarrowia lipolytica yeast biomass, chromium-containing yeast ( Yarrowia lipolytica ) biomass and selenium-containing yeast ( Yarrowia lipolytica ) biomass.'),
('POL-NF-06124', 'Adansonia digitata', 'baobab (ENG, FR, NL), Affenbrotbäume (DE), árbol botella (ES), apenbroodboom (NL), abre bouteille (FR)', null, '[{"part":"Fruit pulp","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Bark, leaves, fruit, seed and root","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the bark, leaves, fruit, seed and root of Adansonia digitata. It belongs to the family of Malvaceae.'),
('POL-NF-11061', 'UV-treated skimmed milk with less than 0,375 μg/100 g vitamin D3.', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns UV-treated skimmed milk with less than 0,375 μg/100 g vitamin D 3 .According to the conclusion reached by the Danish competent authorities (Danish Veterinary and Food Administration (DVFA)) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, UV-treated sk'),
('POL-NF-11201', 'Lactococcus cremoris', 'Lactococcus lactis subsp. cremoris, Streptococcus lactis subsp. cremoris, Streptococcus cremoris', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Lactococcus cremoris bacteria . These bacteria have been used as characteristic ingredients in fermentation of food products'),
('POL-NF-11181', 'Tetradesmus almeriensis', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry is part of a request submitted to the Czech competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 of a number of algal species including Tetradesmus almeriensis Turiel, Garrido-Cardenas, Gómez-Serrano, Acién, Carretero-Paulet & S.Blanco 2021, which are referred to as Scenedesmus sp. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en under the entry Scenedesmus sp.'),
('POL-NF-00735', 'Tanacetum parthenium', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Chrysanthemum parthenium'),
('POL-NF-10463', 'Holothuria scabra', null, 'Sea cucumber', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the French competent authority (General Directorate of food) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Holothuria scabra is considered novel in food .'),
('POL-NF-10462', 'Holothuria whitmaiei', null, 'Sea cucumber', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the French competent authority (General Directorate of food) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Holothuria whitmaiei is considered novel in food .'),
('POL-NF-06181', 'Beta-galactosidase from Aspergillus oryzae', null, null, '[{"part":"Beta-galactosidase from Aspergillus oryzae","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Beta-galactosidase from Aspergillus oryzae is considered not novel in Food Supplement.'),
('POL-NF-00357', 'Ferula hermonis', null, 'pirunpihka (FI)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"SUBJECT_TO_A_CONSULTATION_REQUEST"}]'::jsonb, 'Ferula hermonis belongs to the Umbelliferae Family. Its natural habitat is in south-east Lebanon on the sides of tha Mount Hermon close to the borders of Lebanon, Syria and Israel. The key part of the plant is the root.'),
('POL-NF-13261', 'Boron glycinate and boron bisglycinate', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of boron glycinate and/or boron bisglycinate. The request was submitted to the Czech competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en.'),
('POL-NF-06161', 'Phymatolithon calcareum', 'Millepora calcarea Pallas 1766, Nullipora calcareum (Pallas) Lamarck 1801, Melobesia calcarea (Pallas) Harvey 1849, Spongites calcareus (Pallas) Kützing 1849, Lithothamnion calcareum (Pallas) J.E.Areschoug 1852, Lithophyllum calcareum (Pallas) Foslie 1898, Paraspora calcarea (Pallas) Heydrich 1908', 'DE: Kalkalge', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Phymatolithon calcareum (Pallas) W.H.Adey & D.L.McKibbin ex Woelkering & L.M.Irvine 1986.'),
('POL-NF-09509', 'Euglena gracilis', null, 'Schlankes Augentier (DE)', '[{"part":"Dried biomass","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of dried Euglena gracilis G.A.Klebs 1883.'),
