('POL-NF-10121', 'Eschscholtzia californica', null, 'california poppy, californian poppy, golden poppy, california sunlight, eschscholzia de Californie, pavot jaune de californie; (FR), slaapmutsje, goudpapaver (NL)', '[{"part":"Whole plant","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Eschscholzia californica is a plant belonging to the family of Papaveraceae. A history of consumption in food supplements is available for the aerial parts of the herb including the flower and the root.'),
('POL-NF-10721', 'Edible bird nest', null, null, '[{"part":"Edible bird nest","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the edible bird nest.'),
('POL-NF-00725', 'Stevia rebaudiana', 'Eupatorium rebaudianum Bertoni, Stevia rebaudiana Hemsl.', 'candyleaf, sweetleaf, sugarleaf', '[{"part":"Non-concentrated aqueous infusion (leaves)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of herbal and fruits infusions, tea containing or prepared with leaves of Stevia Rebaudiana (Bertoni) Bertoni which are intended to be consumed as such. It also concerns the use of Stevia Rebaudiana leaves in food supplements. The French competent authority (DGAL) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural step'),
('POL-NF-16421', 'Arachis hypogaea L.', 'Arachis nambyquarae', null, '[{"part":"Protein powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the peanut plant ( Arachis hypogaea L.). The plant belongs to the Fabaceae Family. Concerning the peanut ( Arachis hypogaea L.) protein powder, a request under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283 was submitted to the Dutch Novel Food Unit of the Medicines Evaluation Board Agency. It was considered novel food . The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en'),
('POL-NF-08662', 'Garcinia gummi-gutta (L.) N.Robson', 'Garcinia cambogia', 'CitrinGambooge, guttagomboom (NL), guttier (FR), Garcínia (PT), tamaryndowiec malabarski (PL), Malabar Tamarinde (DE), garcinie kambodžská (CZ), Tamarindo malabar (ES), malabar tamarind (DK), Kambodžas garsīnija (LV), vrsta garcinije (SL)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Exotic fruit (Clusiaceae Family) grown in South India, has been used to impart a distinctive sour flavour to Indian cooking.'),
('POL-NF-09563', 'Haematococcus lacustris', 'Sphaerella lacustris (Girod-Chantrans) Wittrock ex Hansgirg 1888,Haematococcus pluvialis Flotow 1844, Sphaerella wrangelii Sommerfelt1824, Protococcus kermesinus (Wrangel) C.Agardh 1825,Chlorococcumkermesinum (Wrangel) Fries 1825, Byssus kermesina (Wrangel)Wahlenberg1826, Protococcus monospermus Corda 1833, Globulinakermesina(Wrangel) Turpin 1836, Globulina kermesinum (Wrangel) Turpin1836,Disceraea purpurea A.Morren & C.Morren 1841, Haematococcus cordae Meneghini 1843', 'DE: Blutregenalge', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Astaxanthin-rich oleoresin from Haematococcus pluvialis","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Haematococcus lacustris (Girod-Chantrans) Rostafinski 1875'),
('POL-NF-09581', 'Laminaria hyperborea', 'Fucus hyperboreus Gunnerus 1776, Fucus scoparius Ström 1762, Laminaria cloustonii Edmondston 1845, Hafgygia cloustonii (Edmondston) Areschoug 1883, Laminaria hyperborea f. compressa Foslie 1884', 'DE: Palmentang', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Laminaria hyperborea (Gunnerus) Foslie 1885'),
('POL-NF-00446', 'Lactarius deterrimus', null, 'Fichtenreizker (DE)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'see Lactarius deliciosus'),
('POL-NF-00378', 'Gigantochloa albociliata', 'Oxytenanthera albociliata', 'Μπαμπού (GR)', '[{"part":"Steam (botanically immature shoots)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the stem (botanically immature shoot) of Gigantochloa albociliata (Munro) Kurz. Gigantochloa albociliata (Munro) Kurzis one of the edible bamboo species. Gigantochloa is a tropical genus of giant clumping bamboo, similar to the genus Bambusa . It belongs to the plant family Poaceae (Gramineae) and is found in Southeast Asia.'),
('POL-NF-00356', 'Fermented wheat germ extract', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The product is derived from wheat ( Triticum aestivum ) germ fermented with Saccharomyces cerevisiae baker’s yeast. The fermentation medium is extracted with ethyl acetate and -after removal of the solvent- formulated into capsules with excipients.'),
('POL-NF-08821', 'Fish oil', null, null, '[{"part":"Concentrated fish oil high in long chain monounsaturated fatty acids extracted from mackerel and/or herring","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concern concentrated fish oil high in long chain monounsaturated fatty acids extracted from mackerel and/or herring , submitted to the Finnish competent authorities (Finnish Food Authority),under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283.. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was established. Therefore, concentrated fish oil high in long chain monounsaturated fatty acids extracted from mackerel and/or herring is considered not novel in food. The outcome is also pub'),
('POL-NF-00776', 'Vigna sinensis', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Vigna unguiculata'),
('POL-NF-08682', 'Helianthus annuus L.', 'Helianthus annuus f. annuus', 'Sunflower (EN)', '[{"part":"Flowers, seeds (achene) and seed oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves and Flower buds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Protein isolate from sunflower seeds","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Sunflower seed oil (creamy)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"(young) shoots of sunflower","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"High palmitic sunflower oil","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns on one hand the use of flowers, seed (achene), seed oil, leaves and flower buds of Helianthus annuus (sunflower) and on the other hand three requests on three products (protein isolate from sunflower seeds, sunflower seed oil - creamy, and high palmitic sunflower oil) submitted following the provisions of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456. On the first request and according to the conclusion reached by the French competent authorities (DGAL) in response to a req'),
('POL-NF-00525', 'Myrciaria divaricata', null, null, '[{"part":null,"status":null}]'::jsonb, 'see Myrciaria dubia'),
('POL-NF-00767', 'Urtica dioica', 'Urtica galeopsifolia Wierzb. ex Opiz, Urtica tibetica W.T. Wang', 'ES: Ortiga, chichicaste', '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"All plant parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves and all plant parts of Urtica dioica L. . It belongs to the plant family Urticaceae.'),
('POL-NF-08561', 'Zanthoxylum piperitum', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruits of the plant species Zanthoxylum piperitum . According to the conclusion reached by the Spanish food safety and nutrition agency O.A (AESAN O.A), in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, the fruits of the plant species Zanthoxylum '),
('POL-NF-00773', 'Valerianella locusta', null, 'DE: Feldsalat, Rapunzel', '[{"part":"Leaves of Valerianella locusta","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves of Valerianella locusta. Valerianella locusta is a part of the Caprifoliaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00654', 'Richeria grandis', null, 'suur marbripuu (ET)', '[{"part":"Roots and bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Richeria grandis Vahl belongs to the plant family Olacaceae and is native to South America . An alkaloid called ´muirapuamin´ is contained in red part of the inner bark.'),
('POL-NF-00145', 'Arctium lappa', 'Arcion majus Bubani', 'Burdock (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the entire plant Arctium lappa L.'),
('POL-NF-00360', 'Ficus carica', null, null, '[{"part":"Aqueous extract from fig leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The request concerns aqueous extract from fig ( Ficus carica ) L. leaves.According to the conclusion reached by German Federal Office for Consumer Protection and Food Safety (BVL) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, aqueous extract from fig ( Ficus carica ) '),
('POL-NF-08582', 'Casein hydrolysate containing elevated levels of the tri-peptides; L-valyl-L-prolyl-L-proline (VPP) and L-isoleucyl-L-prolyl-L-proline (IPP)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'A spray-dried powdered fraction of casein hydrolysate containing two tri-peptides, L-valyl-L-prolyl-L-proline(VPP)and L-isoleucyl-L-prolyl-L-proline(IPP).'),
('POL-NF-08702', 'Pyropia tenera', 'Porphyra tenera Kjellman 1897, Phyllona tenera (Kjellman) Kuntze 1898, Neopyropia tenera (Kjellman) L.-E.Yang & J.Brodie 2020, Porphyra tenera f. typica Ueda 1932', 'Asakusanori, szkarłatnica delikatna (PL)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Pyropia tenera (Kjellman) N.Kikuchi, M.Miyata, M.S.Hwang & H.G.Choi 2011'),
('POL-NF-00783', 'Volvariella volvacea', 'Agaricus volvaceus Bull., Volvaria volvacea (Bull.) P. Kumm., Volvariopsis volvacea (Bull.) Murrill, Agaricus virgatus Pers.', 'FR: Champignon de paille, volvaire comestible', '[{"part":"Fruiting body","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the fruiting body of Volvariella volvacea .'),
('POL-NF-00252', 'Citrus aurantium', null, 'Pomerans, bitterappelsin (NO)', '[{"part":"Fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Leaves and flowers","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of fruits, leaves and flowers of Citrus aurantium L. . It belongs to the plant family Rutaceae.'),
('POL-NF-08683', 'Creatine monohydrate', null, null, '[{"part":"Creatine monohydrate and micronised creatine monohydrate","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Creatine [N-(aminoiminomethyl-N-methyl glycine)] occurs naturally in foods such as meat, fish and other animal products. It may also be formed endogenously in the liver, kidney and pancreas from the amino acids Gly, Arg and Met. According to the conclusion reached by the German competent authority (German federal state) in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-proc'),
('POL-NF-00148', 'Armoracia rusticana', null, 'Horseradish (EN), Meerrettich, Kren (DE), Cran (FR), Cren, Crenno (IT)', '[{"part":"Roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the roots of Armoracia rusticana. It is a perennial plant of the family Brassicaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00247', 'Chrysanthemum parthenium', 'Tanacetum parthenium (L.) Sch.Bip.', 'Kopretina řimbaba (CZ)', '[{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the aerial parts of Chrysanthemum parthenium (L.) Bernh. It is a perennial plant belonging to the Asteraceae family.'),
('POL-NF-00274', 'Coprinus comatus', null, null, '[{"part":"Dehydrated mycelium powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Coprinus comatus dehydrated mycelium powder. A consultation request was submitted to the Spanish authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, Coprinus comatus dehydrated mycelium powder is considered a novel food.'),
('POL-NF-09601', 'Limnospira fusiformis', 'Spirulina fusiformis Woronichin 1934, Arthrospira fusiformis (Voronichin) Komárek & J.W.G.Lund 1990', 'DE: Spirulina', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Limnospira fusiformis (Voronichin) Nowicka-Krawczyk, Mühlsteinová & Hauer 2019'),
('POL-NF-09602', 'Limnospira indica', 'Arthrospira indica Desikachary & N.Jeeji Bai 1992', 'DE: Spirulina', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Limnospira indica (Desikachary & N.Jeeji Bai) Nowicka-Krawczyk, Mühlsteinová & Hauer 2019'),
('POL-NF-08684', 'Quercus rotundifolia Lam.', null, 'Bolota de Azinheira (PT)', '[{"part":"Fruit (acorn)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the fruit (acorn) of Quercus rotundifolia Lam. It belongs to the plant family Fagaceae.'),
('POL-NF-00663', 'Rubus arcticus', null, 'Åkerbär (SE)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the berry of Rubus arcticus L .. The edible part of Rubus arcticus L. is the berry. Rubus arcticus L. belongs to the plant family Rosaceae .'),
('POL-NF-00761', 'Turnera diffusa', 'Turnera aphrodisiaca Ward', 'turnera rozpierzchła/ damiana (PL)', '[{"part":"Infusion of the leaves and stems","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves and stems for infusion purposes and aerial parts of Turnera diffusa Wild. ex Schult. It belongs to the Turneraceae Family.'),
('POL-NF-12781', 'Pinellia ternata', 'Arisaema loureiroi Blume; Arisaema macrourum (Bunge) Kunth', null, '[{"part":"rhizome and alcohol extract","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of rhizome and alcohol extract of Pinellia ternata.'),
('POL-NF-09242', 'Cordyceps militaris', 'Clavaria gemmata Schaeff., Hypoxylon militare (L.) Mérat, Sphaeria militaris (L.) J.F. Gmel., Xylaria militaris (L.) Gray, Corynesphaera militaris (L.) Dumort.', null, '[{"part":"Mycelium and fruiting body","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the mycelium and fruiting body of Cordyceps militaris. It is a species of fungus belonging to the family Cordycipitaceae.'),
('POL-NF-14381', 'Boesenbergia rotunda', 'Boesenbergia baimaii Saensouk & K.Larsen; Boesenbergia cochinchinensis (Gagnep.) Loes.', 'Boesenbergia rotunda', '[{"part":"Root","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the powder of the root of Boesenbergia rotunda, also known as Fingerroot, Krachai or Chinese Ginger.'),
('POL-NF-15116', 'Carnobacterium maltaromaticum', 'Carnobacterium piscicola', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the microbial culture of Carnobacterium maltaromaticum'),
('POL-NF-15130', 'Kocuria varians', 'Micrococcus varians', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the microbial culture of Kocuria varians'),
('POL-NF-09621', 'Limnospira maxima', 'Arthrospira maxima Setchell & N.L.Gardner 1917, Spirulina maxima (Setchell & N.L.Gardner) Geitler 1932, Oscillatoria pseudoplatensis Bourrelly 1970', 'DE: Spirulina', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Limnospira maxima (Setchell & N.L.Gardner) Nowicka-Krawczyk, Mühlsteinová & Hauer 2019'),
('POL-NF-08863', 'Frangula alnus', 'Frangula dodonei Ard., Rhamnus frangula L.', 'alder buckthorn, glossy buckthorn, or breaking buckthorn (ENG) alder buckthorn (DE), bourdaine, bourgène (FR), sporkehout, vuilboom (NL), arraclán (ES), frangula (IT), Φραγκούλα (GR)', '[{"part":"Bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Herbal infusions of the bark","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Frangula alnus (Synonyms: Frangula dodonei Ard., Rhamnus frangula L) belongs to the family of Rhamnaceae. The bark of Frangula alnus is considered as not novel in food supplements. Herbal infusions of the bark are however considered as novel food.'),
('POL-NF-08921', 'Secale cereale', null, null, '[{"part":"Young shoots","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Finnish food Authority, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, the (young) shoots of rye (Secale cereale) (ryegrass) are considered novel.'),
('POL-NF-08922', 'fish oil VLCPUFA 5', null, null, '[{"part":"whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'According to the conclusion reached by the Norwgian Food Safety Authority, in response to the request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, fish oil with a higher content of very long chain mono- and polyunsaturated fatty acidsis considered not novel.'),
('POL-NF-08901', 'Aquafaba (&quot;chickpea water&quot;)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of the water that beans such as chickpeas have been cooked in. Aquafaba is not considered novel food.'),
('POL-NF-00143', 'Arabinogalactan', null, 'arabinogalaktaan (ET)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the polysaccharide ‘Arabinogalactan’ derived from the wood of the larch tree (Larix species)'),
('POL-NF-00155', 'Artocarpus heterophyllus', 'Artocarpus integrifolius Trimen', 'Jackfrugt (DK)', '[{"part":"Fruit","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns the fruits (sorosus) of Artocarpus heterophyllus. The jackfruit ( Artocarpus heterophyllus or A. heterophylla ) is a species of tree in the Artocarpus genus of the mulberry family (Moraceae).'),
