('POL-NF-00352', 'Fagus sylvatica L.', null, 'EN: European beech, DE: rotbuche, FR: hêtre commun, DK: almindelig bøg, ES: haya común, IT: faggio comune, PT: faia-europeia, NL: beuk, FI: euroopanpyökki, EE: harilik pöök, LT: paprastasis bukas, SE: bok, PL: buk zwyczajny, BG: обикновеният бук, CZ: buk lesní, LV: eiropas dižskābardis, LU: routbuch, RO: fagul, SK: buk lesný, SI: bukev, HU: európai bükk, GR: Oξιά ή δασική οξιά', '[{"part":"Nuts, oil and fruits","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts, gem, wood, wood tar and bark","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the nuts and oil of the nuts, fruits, the aerial parts, gem, wood, wood tar and bark of Fagus sylvatica L..'),
('POL-NF-00694', 'Colloidal silver', 'Silver hydrosol', 'Koloidāls sudrabs (LV)', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Colloidal silver is not a novel food, but it is not authorised as a source of nutrient. Colloidal silver is comprised of silver ions suspended in water and contains silver nanoparticles.'),
('POL-NF-00484', 'Lutein', null, 'λουτεϊνη (EL)', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'Lutein is a natural fat-soluble carotenoid, found in vegetables and fruit, particularly concentrated in green leafy vegetables such as kale, spinach and collard greens. It is a yellow pigment classified as common xanthophylls. Xanthophylls play a critical role in the photosynthetic process. Lutein and its isomer, zeaxanthin, often occur together and lutein can be converted to zeaxanthin in the blood serum.'),
