('POL-NF-00579', 'Perna canaliculus', null, 'slávka zelenoústá (CZ)', '[{"part":"Mussels","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry only concerns Perna canaliculus (Green-lipped mussels), which are found in the oceans of the New Zealand.'),
('POL-NF-09001', 'Glycine max', 'Dolichos sofa L.', null, '[{"part":"Protein hydrolysates","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Heat-treated fermentate","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the protein hydrolysates obtained by the mild acid hydrolysis of Glycine max (L.) Merr. According to the conclusion reached by the Irish Food Safety Authority in response to a request submitted pursuant to the requirements of Commission Implementing Regulation (EU) 2018/456 (https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en) on the procedural steps of the consultation process for determination of novel food status, Soy Protein Hydrolysate is not novel In addi'),
('POL-NF-00774', 'Verbena officinalis L.', null, 'EN: common vervain, DE: echte eisenkraut, FR: verveine officinale, DK: lægejernurt, NL: ijzerhard, ES: verbena común, PT: verbena, SE: järnört, FI: rohtoverbena, PL: werbena pospolita, BG: върбинката, CZ: sporýš lékařský, EE: harilik raudürt, LT: vaistinė verbena, RO: verbina comună, SK: železník lekársky, HU: közönséges vasfű', '[{"part":"Infusion of the leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Aerial parts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts of Verbena officinalis L.. and the use of the leaves in tea, herbal and fruits infusions consumed as such.'),
