('POL-NF-00426', 'Ilex guayusa', 'Ilex utilis Moldenke', null, '[{"part":"All parts of the tree","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Aqueous extract of dried leaves","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns all the parts of the tree of Ilex guayusa Loes. . Species native to Ecuador and distant relative to Mate ( Ilex paraguariensis ). A tall evergreen tree native to the upper Amazonian regions of Ecuador, northeastern Peru, and southwestern Colombia, belonging to the Aquifoliaceae Family. Aqueous extracts of dried leaves of Ilex guayusa is an authorised novel food in herbal infusions and food supplements.'),
