('POL-NF-17304', 'Cystophora cristata', null, 'Hooded seal, Bladdernose seal (EN)', '[{"part":"meat and blubber","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the hooded seal ( Cystophora cristata). The hooded seal is a large seal species occurring in the Arctic and North Atlantic regions. Adult males possess a characteristic inflatable nasal sac and hood-like structure on the head, which gives the species its common name. The placing on the EU market of products derived from seal is subject to Regulation (EC) No 1007/2009 on trade in seal products, which in principle prohibits such products unless the specific conditions in said re'),
