('POL-NF-15347', 'Apigenin', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Apigenin (≥ 98%) isolated from the aerial parts of Matricaria chamomilla L. which was subject to a request “Mixture of plant extracts and purified bioactive substances” under Article 4 to the Czech competent authority. It was considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-15349', 'Pterostilbene', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Pterostilbene (≥ 99%) isolated from the wood of Pterocarpus santalinus L. f. which was subject to a request “Mixture of plant extracts and purified bioactive substances” under Article 4 to the Czech competent authority. It was considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-16002', 'Fisetin', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Fisetin (≥ 98%) isolated from the bark of Cotinus coggygria Scop. which was subject to a request “Mixture of plant extracts and purified bioactive substances” under Article 4 to the Czech competent authority. It was considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-17303', 'Pagophilus groenlandicus', null, 'Harp seal, Greenland seal, Saddleback seal (EN)', '[{"part":"meat and blubber","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the harp seal ( Pagophilus groenlandicus ; former Phoca groenlandica ). The harp seal is a medium-sized Arctic seal native to the North Atlantic Ocean and Arctic Ocean. Adults are characterised by the distinctive dark harp-shaped marking on their back, from which the species derives its common name. It is also known as the Greenland seal or saddleback seal. The placing on the EU market of products derived from seal is subject to Regulation (EC) No 1007/2009 on trade in seal pr'),
('POL-NF-17305', 'Erignathus barbatus', null, 'Bearded seal (EN)', '[{"part":"meat and blubber","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the bearded seal ( Erignathus barbatus ; former Phoca barbata ) The bearded seal is a large Arctic seal distributed throughout Arctic and sub-Arctic waters. The species is recognised by its prominent whiskers, which give rise to its common name. It is associated with sea ice and coastal Arctic marine environments. The placing on the EU market of products derived from seal is subject to Regulation (EC) No 1007/2009 on trade in seal products, which in principle prohibits such pr'),
('POL-NF-14784', 'UV treated wine at dosages up to 3kJ/L', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns wine treated with ultra-violet (UV)-C-light-dosages up to 3kJ/L. The request was submitted to the Danish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
('POL-NF-16041', 'Diplotaxis tenuifolia L.', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves and stems","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the the plant species Diplotaxis tenuifolia L., commonly known as wild arugula. Diplotaxis tenuifolia L. is a perennial herbaceous plant of the family Brassicaceae, native to the Mediterranean region. A request concerning the leaves, stems and seeds of the plant species Diplotaxis tenuifolia L., was submitted to the Spanish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.'),
('POL-NF-14702', 'Lactobacillus paragasseri', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Lactobacillus paragasseri in food supplements.'),
('POL-NF-14867', 'Palmitoylethanolamide (PEA)', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the N -(2-Hydroxyethyl)hexadecanamide.'),
('POL-NF-15161', 'Arginine alpha ketoglutarate (AAKG)', null, 'DE : Arginin-Alpha-Ketoglutarat', '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"}]'::jsonb, 'Arginine alpha-ketoglutarate (AAKG) is a salt of the amino acid arginine and alpha-ketoglutaric acid.'),
('POL-NF-14866', 'Cistanche tubulosa (Schenk) Wight', null, null, '[{"part":"All plant plarts and their extracts","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Cistanche tubulosa. It is a Chinese perennial plant, which belongs to Orobanchaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-15021', 'Benfotiamine', null, null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns benfotiamine, which is a chemically synthesised compound consisting of a derivative of vitamin B1 (thiamine) and a benzoyl group, intended for use as a food supplement. The request was submitted to the Czech competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-status_en'),
