('POL-NF-14703', 'Agaricus subrufescens', 'Agaricus blazei Murrill sensu auct. non sensu Murrill, Agaricus albopersistens Zuccher., Agaricus bambusae Beeli, Agaricus brasiliensis Wasser, M. Didukh, Amazonas & Stamets, Agaricus fiardii Pegler, Psalliota subrufescens (Peck) Kauffman, Agaricus rufotegulis Nauta', 'Hime-matsutake', '[{"part":"Fruiting body","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Dehydrated mycelium powder","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The mushrooms that were previously named Agaricus blazei Murrill are actually Agaricus subrufescens Peck.The name Agaricus blazei Murill refers to a different, non-cultivated mushroom species and should therefore no longer be used. The entry concerns the fruiting body and the dehydrated mycelium powder Agaricus subrufescens Peck. The latter was submitted with the formerly used name Agaricus blazei to the Spanish competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded t'),
('POL-NF-14941', 'Fusarium venenatum', null, null, '[{"part":"mycoprotein of Fusarium venenatum strain A3/5 (NRRL 26139)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"mycoprotein of Fusarium venenatum strain (NRRL 26228)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns a protein-rich preparation (mycoprotein) of a fungus belonging to the family of Nectriaceae. The mycoprotein derived from a specific strain of Fusarium venenatum A3/5 (NRRL 26139, IMI 145425, ATCC PTA-2684) has a history of consumption (aerobic fermentation process from a carbohydrate substrate). It is also important that the process applied during the production of that mycoprotein does not lead to significant changes in the composition, metabolism and undesirable substances.'),
