('POL-NF-16982', 'Oil from Ulkenia sp.', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Specific oil from Ulkenia sp.","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns oil from Ulkenia sp. Ulkenia sp. are often referred to as microalgae for practical or functional reasons. However, they belong to the net slime moulds (Labyrinthulomycetes) and are considered fungus-like organisms.'),
('POL-NF-16981', 'Oils from Schizochytrium sp. and strains of Schizochytrium limacinum', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Specific oils from Schizochytrium sp. and strains of Schizochytrium limacinum","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns different oils from Schizochytrium sp. and from strains of Schizochytrium limacinum. Schizochytrium sp. are often referred to as microalgae for practical or functional reasons. However, they belong to the net slime moulds (Labyrinthulomycetes) and are considered fungus-like organisms.'),
('POL-NF-14061', 'Chenopodium bonus-henricus', null, null, '[{"part":"Leaves","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves of Chenopodium bonus-henricus L. The request was submitted to the Spanish Competent Authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en'),
('POL-NF-13681', 'Creatine malate', null, null, '[{"part":"Substance","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of creatine malate in food. The request was submitted to the Czech competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the history of consumption in the EU was not established. Therefore, creatine malate is considered a novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en.'),
('POL-NF-16941', 'Akkermansia muciniphila', null, null, '[{"part":"Akkermansia muciniphila (pasteurised)","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Akkermansia muciniphila'),
('POL-NF-14382', 'Castanea sativa', 'Castanea castanea (L.) H.Karst.; Castanea prolifera (K.Koch) Hickel.', 'EN: Chestnut', '[{"part":"Fermented chestnuts","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns koji chestnuts ( Castanea sativa) obtained by fermentation with the fungus Aspergillus oryzae. The request was submitted to the Spanish authorities under Article 4 of Regulation(EU) 2015/2283. It was concluded that the chestnuts ( Castanea sativa ) and the fungus Aspergillus oryzae have a history of consumption in the European Union before 15 May 1997 and in the resulting fermentation product, there are no significant changes in the composition or structure of the food affecti'),
('POL-NF-14602', 'Ulva compressa', 'Conferva compressa (Linnaeus) Roth 1797', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the algae Ulva compressa Linnaeus 1753.'),
('POL-NF-17306', 'Chorda filum', null, 'Sea lace, Dead man''s rope, Mermaid''s tresses (EN)', '[{"part":"Whole alga","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the marine brown alga (Phaeophyceae) belonging to the family Chordaceae. Chorda filum is distributed in temperate and cold coastal waters of the North Atlantic and adjacent seas. This entry concerns the consumption of the whole alga and traditional food preparations thereof. The status of extracts, isolated compounds, or products obtained through processing that significantly alters the composition of the alga should be assessed separately on a case-by-case basis. Novel food s'),
('POL-NF-15162', 'Caulerpa lentillifera J.Agardh 1837', 'Ahnfeldtia lentillifera (J.Agardh) Trevisan', 'DE: Umibudo, Meerestraube, Grüner Kaviar', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns algae of the species Caulerpa lentillifera'),
('POL-NF-13863', 'Bromus secalinus', 'Avena secalina (L.) Salisb., Bromus mollis var. secalinus (L.) Huds.', null, '[{"part":"Seeds","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Bromus secalinus seeds'),
('POL-NF-15343', 'Gynostemma pentaphyllum (Thunb.) Makino', null, 'jiaogulan ; EN: sweet tea vine ; FR: herbe de l’immortalité', '[{"part":"Leaf","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Gynostemma pentaphyllum extract (standardized to 80% gypenosides)","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the leaves of Gynostemma pentaphyllum (Thunb.) Makino which belongs to the family of Cucurbitaceae. Gynostemma pentaphyllum extract (standardized to 80% gypenosides) was subject to a request “Mixture of plant extracts and purified bioactive substances” under Article 4 to the Czech competent authority. It was considered novel food. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link: https://food.ec.europa.eu/food-safety/novel-food/consultation-process-novel-food-s'),
('POL-NF-15346', 'Matricaria chamomilla L.', 'Chamomilla recutita (L.) Rausch.', 'DE: Echte Kamille ; EN: chamomile, camomile ; FR: matricaire camomille, camomille vulgaire;', '[{"part":"aerial parts (including flowers)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the aerial parts of Matricaria chamomilla L.. which belongs to the family of Asteraceae. For apigenin see the corresponding entry.'),
