('POL-NF-17302', 'Pusa hispida', null, 'Ringed seal (EN)', '[{"part":"meat and blubber","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the ringed seal ( Pusa hispida ; former Phoca hispida , Phoca foetida ). The ringed seal is a small earless seal species native to Arctic and sub-Arctic regions of the Northern Hemisphere. It is widely distributed throughout the Arctic Ocean and adjacent seas and is characterized by the light ring-shaped markings on its coat. The placing on the EU market of products derived from seal is subject to Regulation (EC) No 1007/2009 on trade in seal products, which in principle prohi'),
('POL-NF-16161', 'Lippia origanoides Kunth', 'Lippia graveolens Kunth', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns Lippia origanoides , a highly aromatic perennial shrub from the Verbenaceae family.'),
('POL-NF-15140', 'Limosilactobacillus fermentum', 'Lactobacillus fermentum', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the microbial culture of Limosilactobacillus fermentum'),
('POL-NF-16101', 'Acidipropionibacterium acidipropionici', 'Propionibacterium acidipropionici', null, '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of A cidipropionibacterium acidipropionici bacteria . These bacteria have been used as characteristic ingredients in fermentation of food products'),
('POL-NF-15901', 'Clupea harengus L.', null, 'EN: Herring', '[{"part":"Oil extracted from roe","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'A consultation request concerning herring ( Clupea harengus L.) roe oil was submitted to the Norwegian authorities under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en under the entry “Herring ( Clupea harengus L.) roe oil”'),
('POL-NF-17082', 'Echinacea angustifolia DC.', null, null, '[{"part":"Herbs and roots","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD_SUPPLEMENTS"},{"part":"Non-concentrated aqueous infusion (herbs and roots)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Extract from cell cultures","status":"AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the herbs and roots of Echinacea angustifolia DC. In addition, the entry concerns Echinacea angustifolia and its extract from cell cultures.'),
('POL-NF-17081', 'Musa spp.', null, null, '[{"part":"Fruit pulp (ripe, overripe, or green pulp)","status":"NOT_NOVEL_IN_FOOD"},{"part":"Fruit peel","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"},{"part":"Fruit blossom","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the fruit pulp, peel and blossom of the cultivars of Musa acuminata , Musa × paradisiaca and related edible hybrids , commonly known as banana. The plant belongs to the family Musaceae . A request was submitted to the Portuguese competent authority under Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2015/2283. The outcome is also published on the following Commission''s link https://ec.europa.eu/food/safety/novel_food/consultation-process_en For Musa acuminata Colla see the corresponding entry.'),
('POL-NF-17128', 'Tetrapleura tetraptera', null, 'Aidan-fruit, prekese', '[{"part":"Whole","status":"NOT_YET_AUTHORISED_NOVEL_FOOD"}]'::jsonb, 'The entry concerns the use of Tetrapleura tetraptera (Schumach. & Thonn.) Taub.')
